 code (Terraform cloud formation etc.) to apply changes. Write script to extract cloud security data point for global reporting e.g. python, Review and assess cloud security findings (permissions, misconfigurations, detections), out of box vendor rules, accuracy of detection and identify false positives to fine tune the solution. Partner with cloud architects, DevOps, IT Service owners, and SOC teams to ensure cloud security controls are met, and support incidents management when required. Requirements Hands on experience with cloud native application security solution and cloud security posture management tools e.g. CrowdStrike, Wiz, Orca, Prisma cloud Cyber security experience with cloud security (AWS, GCP, Azure, AliCloud) risks and controls does a violation present a material risk, why and potential impact. Strong collaboration and stakeholders management Experience in building and deploying applications on the Cloud, using CI/CD frameworks and Infrastructure automation, such as: Jenkins, Terraform, Ansible, GitHub, Nexus and Jenkins. Extensive working knowledge of software development tools and technologies; specifically, Python, Bash, PowerShell, SQL, and data formats such as XML, JSON, CSV Nice to have: CSP security certificate e.g. AWS/GCP/Azure certified security speciality,\n\nKey Skills: Cloud Security,CNAPP,Cyber security,Infrastructure Automation,Cloud native application security,PowerShell,Azure,Orca"},{"title":"OSB Oracle SOA suite","company":"Purview Services","location":"Kolkata","date_posted":"2026-09-16","url":"https://www.naukri.com/job-listings-osb-oracle-soa-suite-purview-services-kolkata-6-to-10-years-160926916993","source":"naukri","experience":"6-10 Yrs","skills":[12,102,103],"is_walkin":false,"description":"Role & responsibilities \n Primary Skills description Minimum 6 years experience in designing ESB\u00a0 Extensive hands on with Oracle Service Bus\n Oracle Fusion\u00a0 SOA Suite 10g11g12C WebLogic Server 103x Oracle Adapters like DB B2B File and FTP JMS BPEL ESBMediator Oracle Service Bus Human Workflow BAM BPM \nShould have worked on various versions in Oracle Products and SOA 12C11g10g for defining software engineering at all the stages of SDLC and Agile processes\nKnowledge in functional and technical aspects of SOA Service Oriented Architecture\nDesigning oracle service bus enterprise wide integration backbone\u00a0\n Excellent experience in XML technologies XML XSD XSLT XPath and Web Services SOAP WSDL \nShould have worked on oracle BPEL Process Manager of Oracle SOA Suite which enables enterprises to orchestrate disparate applications and web services into business processes\nThe existing standards and best practices documents for the development and support of Oracle SOA and OSB based services\nTo design the necessary process documentation and templates Secondary Skills MQ series TIBCO EBS integration application server Secondary Skills description Extensive experience in Oracle EBS EBusiness Suite SQL PLSQL SQLPlus OAM OID JDeveloper \nUnderstands Oracle Application Server and Webservers SOA Services Oracle middleware\nShould have experience in all phases of software development lifecycle from gathering requirements to documentation testing implementation and support\nSkills in meeting deadlines in challenging environments operating with clients and internal teams\nSkilled in working with virtual teams across cultures and organisational disciplines\nExperience in building excellent professional relationships\nA flexible and adaptable approach with the ability to multitask within a dynamic environment\nAbility to share information transfer knowledge and expertise to team members\nGood written and oral communication fluent in English writtenverbal additional languages are an advantage\nOracle BPM\u00a0 SOA expert Should be an expert in Oracle BPM rules design and optimization for requisitions Payables Invoices Expenses Purchase Orders etc \nAt least 23 project experience in BPM rules with very complex requirements\nAbility to understand the business requirements and convert them in scalable BPM rules\nGood interpersonal skills expected \n Key Responsibilities \nParticipate in technical and functional design\nParticipate in preparation of low level design documentation\nGood understanding of the product features and its technology platform to assemble a Business Solution\nProactively create documentary artefacts like system integration specifications requirement specifications\nSupport various testing phases SIT UAT etc throughout the implementation\nDefect fixing during testing phases\n\nKey Skills: Oracle BPEL,Oracle Service Bus,XML,Adapters,Oracle SOA,XPath,Oracle SOA Suite,XSD"},{"title":"Senior OSB  / SOA Integration Specialist","company":"Purview Services","location":"Kolkata","date_posted":"2026-09-16","url":"https://www.naukri.com/job-listings-senior-osb-soa-integration-specialist-purview-services-kolkata-6-to-11-years-160926917307","source":"naukri","experience":"6-11 Yrs","skills":[12,102,103],"is_walkin":false,"description":"Role & responsibilities Minimum 6 years experience in designing ESB\u00a0 Extensive hands on with Oracle Service Bus\nOracle Fusion\u00a0 SOA Suite 10g11g12C WebLogic Server 103x Oracle Adapters like DB B2B File and FTP JMS BPEL ESBMediator Oracle Service Bus Human Workflow BAM BPM \nShould have worked on various versions in Oracle Products and SOA 12C11g10g for defining software engineering at all the stages of SDLC and Agile processes\nKnowledge in functional and technical aspects of SOA Service Oriented Architecture\n Designing oracle service bus enterprise wide integration backbone\u00a0\nExcellent experience in XML technologies XML XSD XSLT XPath and Web Services SOAP WSDL \nShould have worked on oracle BPEL Process Manager of Oracle SOA Suite which enables enterprises to orchestrate disparate applications and web services into business processes\nThe existing standards and best practices documents for the development and support of Oracle SOA and OSB based services\nTo design the necessary process documentation and templates Secondary Skills MQ series TIBCO EBS integration application server Secondary Skills description Extensive experience in Oracle EBS EBusiness Suite SQL PLSQL SQLPlus OAM OID JDeveloper \n Understands Oracle Application Server and Webservers SOA Services Oracle middleware \nShould have experience in all phases of software development lifecycle from gathering requirements to documentation testing implementation and support\nSkills in meeting deadlines in challenging environments operating with clients and internal teams\nSkilled in working with virtual teams across cultures and organisational disciplines\nExperience in building excellent professional relationships\nA flexible and adaptable approach with the ability to multitask within a dynamic environment\nAbility to share information transfer knowledge and expertise to team members\nGood written and oral communication fluent in English writtenverbal additional languages are an advantage\nOracle BPM\u00a0 SOA expert Should be an expert in Oracle BPM rules design and optimization for requisitions Payables Invoices Expenses Purchase Orders etc\nAt least 23 project experience in BPM rules with very complex requirements\nAbility to understand the business requirements and convert them in scalable BPM rules\nGood interpersonal skills expected Key Responsibilities \nParticipate in technical and functional design\nParticipate in preparation of low level design documentation\nGood understanding of the product features and its technology platform to assemble a Business Solution\nProactively create documentary artefacts like system integration specifications requirement specifications\nSupport various testing phases SIT UAT etc throughout the implementation\nDefect fixing during testing phases\n\nKey Skills: Web Logic X,Oracle Service Bus,BPEL,Oracle SOA,BPM,XML,WSDL,OSB"},{"title":"Robotic Intern","company":"Fx31 Labs","location":"Ahmedabad","date_posted":"2026-09-17","url":"https://www.naukri.com/job-listings-robotic-intern-fx31-labs-ahmedabad-0-to-1-years-160626015729","source":"naukri","skills":[1,5,28,34,41,103,116],"is_walkin":false,"description":"We have an exciting opportunity for students looking to kick-start their careers. Please review the Job Description shared below and apply if your skills and interests align with the role. \n Position: \u00a0Robotics Intern Autonomous Systems & Prototype Development (Internship)\n Location: \u00a0Ahmedabad (Fx31Labs Office)\n Address: \u00a0205, Amrakunj Avis, Near Tapovan Circle, Above Gwalbhog Restaurant, Chandkheda, Ahmedabad, Gujarat 382424 \n Job Description: Fx31Labs is seeking a passionate and hands-on Robotics Intern Autonomous Systems & Prototype Development \u00a0to join our advanced robotics team. This internship offers a fast-paced, end-to-end engineering experience involving aerial robotics, embedded systems, autonomous navigation, perception, and real-world prototype development.This role is ideal for students and early-career engineers looking to gain practical experience in designing, building, testing, and improving autonomous robotic platforms. \n Key Responsibilities: Design & Build Assemble and integrate motors, ESCs, sensors, flight controllers, microcontrollers, and communication modules. Design and prototype electronic systems for rapid testing and development. Assist in mechanical assembly, wiring, and hardware integration of robotic platforms. Embedded Systems & Control Develop Python and C/C++ software for sensor integration, control systems, and autonomous behaviors. Interface with hardware using UART, CAN, IC, SPI, USB, and wireless communication protocols. Implement safety mechanisms, telemetry systems, and fault-detection routines. Autonomous Navigation & Perception Integrate sensors such as IMUs, GPS, LiDAR, cameras, depth sensors, and range finders. Develop and test localization, navigation, and obstacle-avoidance capabilities. Work with computer vision and perception pipelines for environmental awareness. ROS 2 & SLAM Implement and tune SLAM and localization frameworks using ROS 2. Work with tools such as Cartographer, RTAB-Map, Nav2, and related autonomy stacks. Support mapping, path planning, and autonomous mission execution. System Integration & Testing Integrate hardware, firmware, and software into a fully functional robotic system. Perform debugging, troubleshooting, and validation across electronics, software, and mechanical subsystems. Conduct field testing and analyze system performance. Rapid Prototyping & Iteration Build, test, evaluate, and refine prototypes through iterative development cycles. Document experiments, test results, and design improvements. Contribute innovative ideas to improve system reliability and performance. Team Collaboration Collaborate closely with robotics, embedded, AI, mechanical, and software engineers. Participate in design reviews, sprint planning, testing sessions, and technical discussions. Present findings, challenges, and proposed solutions to the engineering team. \n Qualifications: Pursuing or recently completed a Bachelor's degree in Robotics, Mechatronics, Electronics, Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, Aerospace Engineering, or a related field. Hands-on experience with robotics, embedded systems, drones, autonomous vehicles, or related projects. Proficiency in Python and basic C/C++ programming. Understanding of sensors, control systems, communication protocols, and microcontroller-based development. Experience with hardware assembly, wiring, debugging, and soldering. Comfortable working on both software and physical hardware systems. \n Nice-to-Haves: Experience with ROS 2 and robotic middleware. Knowledge of SLAM, localization, path planning, and autonomous navigation. Experience with PX4, ArduPilot, MAVLink, or similar robotics/autonomy frameworks. Familiarity with OpenCV, computer vision, or AI-based perception systems. Experience with Linux (Ubuntu) development environments. Familiarity with CAD tools such as Fusion 360, SolidWorks, or Onshape. Understanding of wireless communication systems and telemetry. \n Soft Skills: Self-driven and highly proactive. Strong analytical and troubleshooting abilities. Curious mindset with a passion for building real-world robotic systems. Ability to learn quickly and adapt in a rapid prototyping environment. Strong communication and teamwork skills. \n Why Join Us? End-to-End Engineering Experience: \u00a0 Work on complete autonomous robotic systems from design and prototyping to testing and deployment. Advanced Robotics Exposure: \u00a0 Gain hands-on experience in embedded systems, aerial robotics, autonomous navigation, perception, and ROS 2-based autonomy. Learning & Mentorship: \u00a0 Collaborate with experienced engineers and receive practical guidance in real-world R&D projects. Innovation-Driven Environment: \u00a0 Be part of a team focused on rapid prototyping, experimentation, and cutting-edge technology development. \n Internship Details: Duration: \u00a03\u20136 Months\n Type: \u00a0Internship with mentorship, certification, and learning opportunities\n Location: \u00a0On-site at Fx31Labs, Ahmedabad \n About Fx31Labs: Fx31Labs is an innovation-driven tech company delivering solutions at the intersection of robotics, AI, and software development. We specialize in building intelligent, scalable, and automation-first systems for startups and enterprises alike."},{"title":"Sr. Embedded Hardware Engineer","company":"Rudr Consultancy Services","location":"Ahmedabad","date_posted":"2026-09-16","url":"https://www.naukri.com/job-listings-sr-embedded-hardware-engineer-rudr-consultancy-services-ahmedabad-4-to-9-years-160926935960","source":"naukri","experience":"4-9 Yrs","skills":[41,100,103],"is_walkin":false,"description":"Sr. Embedded Hardware Engineer . Job Name: Sr. Embedded Hardware Engineer . Job Role: Delivery Ma