 landing pages, event pages, organic social). This is an individual\\-contributor role for someone who can bring knowledge of best practices and plan and run campaigns independently while working with global stakeholders. This role suits someone who wants ownership over the full digital funnel from ad spend and targeting through to the landing experience, email nurture, and performance reporting. What You'll Do Campaign Execution (Paid Media)\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \u2022 Plan and execute digital campaigns across LinkedIn Ads, Google Search, and other relevant platforms, from budget allocation and audience targeting/filtering through to launch, optimization, and iteration\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Plan, run and manage Search campaigns and potentially AEO (Answer Engine Optimization) ad campaigns\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Own campaign performance: monitor, analyze, and iterate on live campaigns to improve efficiency and results\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Use Salesforce data to identify how prospects have engaged across campaigns and tie together loose ends in the funnel (e.g., connecting ad/campaign touches to pipeline activity, spotting drop\\-off points, following up on gaps in engagement tracking)\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Build and share regular performance reporting, with clear takeaways and recommendations, not just raw numbers\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Identify and share best practices across campaign types and platforms to continuously raise the bar\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Coordinate with third\\-party vendors and agencies supporting digital advertising (media buys, platform reps, ad ops support) Email Marketing \u2022 Build and manage email marketing campaigns in Apollo\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Build and maintain email lists using Salesforce data, working with sales operations to clean and validate lists \u2022 Plan and execute email sends/nurture sequences, monitor performance, and iterate Digital Properties C Organic Social\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Own website performance and metrics (traffic, conversion, page speed). Monitor, report, and flag issues or opportunities\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Own organic social media metrics and reporting\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Handle simple, direct content edits on the website (WordPress) such as copy updates, campaign\\-specific landing page tweaks, and content refreshes. Work alongside our web developer agency for anything beyond direct edits (new pages, complex builds, structural changes)\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Manage cookie/consent configurations and campaign\\-specific tracking setups (UTMs, pixels, conversion tracking)\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Own web form setup and handling for campaign and content assets\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Manage on\\-page SEO / AEO for existing content (metadata, keywords, internal linking, content refreshes)\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Publish and maintain blog content within the existing site structure\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Create and retire event landing pages tied to campaigns, webinars, and conferences\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Coordinate with the web developer agency on anything requiring development work, and work cross\\-functionally with Content, Design, and Marketing Operations to keep digital properties current What You Bring\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 4\u20135 years of hands\\-on experience running digital campaigns across LinkedIn Ads and Google Search (Ads/AEO); B2B experience preferred\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Working knowledge of WordPress specifically\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Experience with Salesforce (or similar CRM), comfortable pulling and interpreting data to trace prospect engagement across campaigns\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Experience with email marketing platforms (Apollo experience a plus) \\- building lists, segmenting, and running campaigns\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Familiarity with web analytics tools (GA4 or equivalent) and organic social analytics, with ability to translate data into reporting and next steps\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Understanding of cookie/consent management and basic campaign tracking setup\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Experience coordinating with external vendors/agencies (media, web development)\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Very hands on, comfortable working independently and owning outcomes.\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Strong communication skills; ability to work across time zones with North American and European stakeholders, and cross\\-functionally with Content, Design, and Operations teams\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Detail\\-oriented, organized, and able to manage multiple concurrent campaigns and site updates without dropping balls What This Role Is Not\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Not a creative/design role \u2014 you'll work with existing creative assets, not produce them\n \n\n\n\n \u2022 Not a web development role \u2014 net\\-new pages, CMS architecture, and complex technical builds go through our web developer agency; you'll handle simple, direct edits and coordinate with the agency on the rest","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468393841","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468393841"},{"title":"Performance Marketing Executive","company":"Tesor Designs","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467517460","source":"linkedin","experience":"2 Yrs","skills":[105,107,108],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**Company Description:** \n Tesor Designs is dedicated to creating homes that inspire and delight every time clients step inside. The company offers turnkey interior design, modular interiors, and custom elements tailored to individual lifestyles and preferences. From design conceptualization to sourcing furnishings and accessories, Tesor Designs manages end\\-to\\-end project execution. Team members collaborate closely with clients, ensuring a seamless experience while turning their dream homes into reality. The work environment values creativity, attention to detail, and a strong focus on customer satisfaction.\n \n\n\n\n**Role Description:** \n The ideal candidate will manage lead generation \\& digital performance marketing activities (paid \\& organic) for Tesor Designs by planning and executing 