Arpit Jain \\[CEO] is a leading ad\\-tech company that's been driving app growth and monetization\n* We\u2019ve built a sustainable and profitable business for over 7 years without chasing vanity metrics and successfully completed our 0\u21921 journey, we\u2019re now scaling rapidly (1\u219210 phase)\n* As a Google Publishing Partner, we serve 100M\\+ daily ad impressions and support 5,000\\+ apps and games worldwide\u2014delivering up to 75% revenue uplift\n* Trusted by brands like Amazon,Sharechat,Treebo, Mobikwik, and 1000\\+ publishers across 20\\+ countries.\n\n\n We are looking for an experienced Account\\-Based Marketing (ABM) professional to develop and execute targeted marketing programs for strategic enterprise accounts. The ideal candidate will partner closely with Sales to drive account engagement, generate qualified pipeline, and support revenue growth through personalized marketing initiatives.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Key Responsibilities**\n* Develop and execute one\\-to\\-one and one\\-to\\-few ABM campaigns for strategic accounts.\n* Partner with Sales to identify target accounts, define account strategies, and align marketing initiatives with business goals.\n* Create personalized campaigns and messaging across digital, email, LinkedIn, webinars, events, and other relevant channels.\n* Collaborate with Product Marketing, Content, and Design teams to develop account\\-specific marketing assets.\n* Monitor campaign performance, analyze engagement, and optimize programs to improve pipeline impact and ROI.\n* Stay updated on industry trends, customer needs, and competitive insights to strengthen ABM strategies.\n\n\n**Experience \\& Qualifications**\n* With 3 years\\+ years of experience in B2B marketing, with a strong focus on Account\\-Based Marketing (ABM) in AdTech, MarTech is a must.\n* Proven experience planning and executing ABM campaigns for enterprise customers.\n* Experience working closely with Sales teams to drive pipeline generation and revenue growth.\n* Prior experience in AdTech, MarTech, SaaS, or a technology\\-driven B2B organization is strongly preferred.\n* Experience marketing to advertisers, agencies, brands, publishers, or commerce/media platforms is an advantage.\n* Strong analytical skills with the ability to evaluate campaign performance and derive actionable insights.\n* Excellent stakeholder management, project management, and communication skills.\n\n\n \ud83c\udf1f What Makes You a Great Fit\n   \n\n  \n\n* You have a proven track record of driving pipeline and revenue through Account\\-Based Marketing programs.\n* You think commercially and align marketing strategies with business and revenue objectives.\n* You partner effectively with Sales to engage target accounts and accelerate deal progression.\n* You use data and account insights to optimize campaigns and maximize ROI.\n* You thrive in a fast\\-paced environment, balancing strategic thinking with flawless execution.\n\n\n \ud83c\udf81 Why GreedyGame?\n   \n\n  \n\n* Opportunity to work on products used by millions \u2013 see: Pubscale\n* Ownership from Day 1 \u2013 shape architecture, strategy, and key decisions\n* Learning stipend for books, courses, and conferences (we love curious minds!) internal blogs\n* A high\\-growth, inclusive, and engineering\\-led culture that supports experimentation and impact\n\n\n Skills: account\\-based marketing,campaigns,b2b marketing","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467549018","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467549018"},{"title":"Digital Marketing Executive","company":"The Yellow Dwelling","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467186184","source":"linkedin","experience":"3 Yrs","skills":[103,107,117],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**Digital Marketing Executive** \n\n\n The Yellow Dwelling is an all\\-natural, contemporary home furnishings brand specialising in 100% cotton and linen products, with 8 retail stores and a growing D2C presence across India.\n \n\n\n\n\n\n We are looking for a creative and enthusiastic Digital Marketing Executive to manage our brand\u2019s digital presence across Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, Google, Pinterest and LinkedIn.\n \n\n\n\n**Responsibilities** \n* Curate and manage the monthly content calendar across social media platforms.\n* Coordinate with freelance photographers and videographers for photoshoots and content creation.\n* Create, edit and publish engaging content(static \\& videos) for social media.\n* Maintain the overall look, feel, aesthetic and creative language of the brand across social media.\n* Manage influencer collaborations end\\-to\\-end.\n* Support the team in planning and executing digital and brand campaigns and shoots.\n\n\n**Skills \\& Experience** \n* 2\u20133 years of experience in digital marketing with a minimum of 1 year in social media marketing.\n* Excellent written and verbal communication skills.\n* Strong creative skills with a good understanding of social media trends and content formats.\n* A strong eye for aesthetics, visual storytelling and brand consistency.\n* Hands\\-on experience with Canva, Filmora and other photo/video editing software.\n* Interior styling/home decor experience will be an added advantage.\n* A degree with relevant social media experience is preferred.\n\n\n\n**Job Type:** \n\n Full\\-time, Permanent\n \n\n\n\n\n**Location:** \n\n Kalyan Nagar, Bengaluru (Near Jal Vayu Vihar)\n \n\n\n\n\n**Work Model:** \n\n Work from Office\n \n\n\n\n\n**Salary:** \n\n \u20b94\\.5 \u2013 \u20b95\\.5 lakhs per annum\n \n\n\n\n\n**Benefits:** \n\n Health Insurance, PF Benefits, Gratuity","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467186184","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467186184"},{"title":"Influencer Marketing Manager","company":"Meolaa","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467188788","source":"linkedin","experience":"4 Yrs","skills":[105,107],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**Influencer Marketing Manager** \n\n\n\n\n We're not hiring someone to spam micro\\-influencers with free products. We need someone who builds real relationships with creators, sources authentic UGC, and turns creator content into a growth lever for HIRA and our portfolio brands.\n \n\n\n\n The role is\n **Influencer Marketing Manager.** \n\n\n\n\n The reality is \u2014 you own community, creator partnerships, and UGC that actually converts.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**What You'll Own** \n\n\n\n\n**Creator Sourcing \\& Outreach** \n\n\n\n* Find micro\\-influencers who actually fit the brand (not just follower count)\n* Build relationships with creators \u2014 be someone they want to work with again\n* Pitch partnerships that feel authentic, not transactional\n* Negotiate rates and deliverables without overpaying\n\n\n\n**UGC \\& Content Strategy** \n\n\n\n* Brief creators on what to make and why (product features, brand story, lifestyle angle)\n* Ensure content works both organically and as paid ads\n* Source unboxing, testimonial, and lifestyle UGC\n* Repurpose creator content into Meta/Google ads with performance tracking\n\n\n\n**Campaign Management** \n\n\n\n* Run influencer campaigns end\\-to\\-end (briefing \u2192 content \u2192 posting \u2192 tracking)\n* Manage timelines and deliverables\n* Handle affiliate/promo code tracking\n* Build repeat creator relationships \u2014 lock in people who work\n\n\n\n**Performance \\& Analytics** \n\n\n\n* Track creator content performance (engagement, reach, saves, conversions)\n* Know which creators drive actual sales vs vanity metrics\n* Build creator cohort analysis \u2014 what type of creator works best?\n* Optimize spend based on creator ROI\n\n\n\n**Community Building** \n\n\n\n* Engage with creator communities \u2014 be present, responsive\n* Foster brand advocates who want to work with you repeatedly\n* Handle DMs, comments, and community feedback\n* Build a \"creator network\" that feels like a community, not a vendor list\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**You might be the one if \u2014** \n\n\n\n* You have 2\u20134 years influencer marketing experience in D2C, beauty, or lifestyle\n* You've managed creator relationships and built repeat partnerships\n* You understand Instagram algorithm \u2014 why some content pops, why some doesn't\n* You know the difference between an influencer and an actual fit for your brand\n* You've sourced and negotiated with micro\\-influencers (the real ROI lies here)\n* You've tracked UGC performance and optimized for actual conversions\n* You're comfortable with social media \u2014 you spend time on Instagram, you know trends\n* Prior experience in fragrance, beauty, or FMCG D2C is a plus\n* You think like a curator, not a marketer \u2014 you're finding people, not broadcasting\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Why Meolaa:** \n\n\n\n\n Meolaa is launching with influencers as a core channel. You'll own creator relationships, UGC strategy, and community building from day one. You're not supporting someone else's strategy \u2014 you're building it.\n \n\n\n\n You'll work with the Growth team to repurpose your UGC into paid ads. You'll have real budget. And you'll see direct impact when creator content drives conversions.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467188788","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467188788"},{"title":"Marketing Analyst","company":"Tredence Inc.","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467999522","source":"linkedin","skills":[7,33,106,107],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**JOB DESCRIPTION** \n\n\n\n\n**CRM Journey Execution \\& Automation Specialist** \n\n\n\n\n**1\\. Role Purpose** \n\n\n\n\n we are looking for an experienced CRM execution specialist to take ownership of the end\\-to\\-end execution and coordination of CRM journeys, with a particular focus on trigger ideation and journey build. The resource will work directly with the VP Pricing and Customer Value Proposition and act as the accountable execution owner for identifying and translating defined CRM use cases, audiences, filters and business requirements into live journeys in Microsoft Dynamics / the relevant CRM environment. The role combines hands\\-on journey execution, stakeholder coordination, process management, reporting and continuous improvement.\n \n\n\n\n**2\\. Key Responsibilities** \n\n\n\n* Own the execution of CRM journeys from defined business requirements through build, approval, launch and monitoring.\n* Translate offline\\-defined journeys, audience criteria and filters into executable CRM journeys and workflows.\n* Configure journey workflows, channel routing, eligibility logic, exclusions and other execution rules in Microsoft Dynamics / CRM tooling.\n* Follow up proactively on all dependencies and approvals across the CRM execution process, ensuring actions are completed on time.\n* Work closely with the team to identify and shape new CRM use cases based on customer events, target segments and commercial objectives.\n* Build a strong understanding of retail banking products, including savings, personal loans, auto loans, mortgages and remittances, and how CRM activity contributes to revenue, customer engagement and profitability.\n* Take accountability for the operational CRM trigger / automation tracker and improve the existing legacy Excel\\-based setup.\n* Maintain clear reporting on journey status, delivery, conversion, errors, performance and key operational KPIs.\n* Develop and maintain performance dashboards and management reporting to provide transparency on CRM activity and outcomes.\n* Support final journey checks covering content, audience, controls, exclusions and readiness before launch.\n* Monitor live journeys and identify execution issues, errors or performance concerns; coordinate resolution with relevant teams.\n* Support optimization of targeting, timing, content, offers and journey logic based on performance results, in partnership with the analytics / optimization team.\n* Act as the day\\-to\\-day accountable owner for CRM journey execution, ensuring initiatives do not stall between ideation and go\\-live.\n\n\n\n**3\\. Minimum Requirements** \n\n\n\n* 7\\+ years of relevant experience in CRM, customer lifecycle management, marketing automation, campaign execution or digital engagement, preferably in retail banking.\n* Hands\\-on experience building and executing CRM journeys in Microsoft Dynamics 365 / Microsoft CRM or a comparable enterprise CRM / marketing automation platform.\n* Strong understanding of journey orchestration, audience segmentation, eligibility rules, filters, exclusions, triggers, channel routing and workflow configuration.\n* Practical understanding of retail banking products and customer journeys; experience with savings, personal loans, auto loans, mortgages and/or remittances is strongly preferred.\n* Ability to independently manage execution from business requirement through CRM build and go\\-live.\n* Strong stakeholder management and follow\\-up skills across multiple teams and dependencies.\n* Strong Excel skills, including ability to structure, clean up and improve complex operational trackers and build management reporting.\n* Comfortable working with data, performance metrics and dashboards; able to interpret results and translate them into execution actions.\n* Strong attention to detail, ownership mindset and ability to manage multiple CRM initiatives simultaneously.\n* Able to operate independently in a complex, multi\\-stakeholder banking environment and proactively identify what needs to happen next.\n\n\n\n**6\\. Preferred Experience** \n\n\n\n* Experience with large regional / international banks.\n* Experience with Microsoft Dynamics / MCD or similar CRM platforms, including production journey go\\-live.\n* Experience in CRM automation, trigger\\-based marketing, lifecycle campaigns or next\\-best\\-action environments.\n* Experience working with retail banking commercial objectives and understanding how CRM initiatives contribute to top\\-line and bottom\\-line impact.\n* Experience partnering with analytics teams on campaign performance, optimization and test\\-and\\-learn.\n* Experience managing CRM operating trackers, dashboards and governance processes.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467999522","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467999522"},{"title":"Influencer Marketing Specialist","company":"GIVA","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468619196","source":"linkedin","experience":"4 Yrs","skills":[103,107],"is_walkin":false,"description":"Influencer Marketing Specialist\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Location:** \n Bangalore\n \n\n\n\n**Experience:** \n 2\u20134 Years\n \n\n\n\n**Employment Type:** \n Full\\-Time\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Job Description\n \n\n\n\n We are looking for an experienced\n **Influencer Marketing Specialist** \n to manage and execute influencer marketing campaigns for GIVA. The role will focus on influencer sourcing, relationship management, campaign execution, content coordination, and performance analysis to strengthen brand visibility and engagement.\n \n\n\n\n Key Responsibilities\n \n\n\n* Identify, research, and onboard relevant influencers across Instagram, YouTube, and other social media platforms.\n* Manage influencer outreach, communication, negotiations, and collaborations.\n* Plan and execute influencer marketing campaigns aligned with brand and marketing objectives.\n* Coordinate with influencers, agencies, and internal teams to ensure timely content delivery.\n* Manage influencer partnerships, deliverables, budgets, and campaign timelines.\n* Track and analyze campaign performance, including reach, engagement, views, conversions, and ROI.\n* Monitor influencer trends and identify new opportunities for brand collaborations.\n* Build and maintain strong relationships with influencers, agencies, and content creators.\n* Prepare campaign performance reports and identify opportunities to improve future campaigns.\n\n\n\n Ideal Candidate Profile\n \n\n\n* **2\u20134 years of experience** \n in Influencer Marketing, Digital Marketing, Social Media Marketing, or a related field.\n* Candidates from the\n **Fashion, Jewellery, Beauty, or Lifestyle industry** \n are preferred.\n* Strong experience in influencer sourcing, outreach, campaign execution, and relationship management.\n* Excellent negotiation, communication, and coordination skills.\n* Strong understanding of social media platforms, influencer trends, and content performance metrics.\n* Experience in campaign analytics, reporting, and performance optimization.\n* Ability to manage multiple influencer campaigns and meet deadlines.\n* Strong organizational and problem\\-solving skills.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468619196","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468619196"},{"title":"Social Media Content Creator","company":"Waxys","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467503593","source":"linkedin","skills":[103,107,115],"is_walkin":false,"description":"Content Marketer\n \n**Full\\-Time \\| On\\-Site \\| Bengaluru** \n\n\n\n\n**If your camera roll is full of random content ideas, half\\-shot reels, references, memes, hooks, scripts, and \u201cwe should totally make this\u201d moments\u2026** \n\n\n\n\n**You\u2019ll probably fit right in.** \n\n\n\n So, what is Atomnia?\n \n Atomnia is the\n **marketing and creative wing of Waxys** \n .\n \n\n\n\n Waxys is a home\\-fragrance brand building products that make everyday spaces smell better and feel better through fragrances, wax melts, and electric aroma solutions.\n \n\n\n\n Atomnia grew out of the marketing engine behind Waxys.\n \n\n\n\n Instead of keeping that creative system limited to one brand, Atomnia now works across\n **content, branding, social media, performance marketing, influencer marketing, photography, video production, and digital campaigns** \n \u2014 for Waxys, other brands, and our own creator\\-led content properties.\n \n\n\n\n Think of it like this:\n \n\n\n\n**Waxys builds products. Atomnia builds attention around them \u2014 and now does the same for much more than Waxys.** \n\n\n\n Your Role\n \n We\u2019re looking for a\n **Content Marketer** \n .\n \n\n\n\n Part marketer.\n \n\n\n\n Part creator.\n \n\n\n\n Part internet addict.\n \n\n\n\n Part \u201cwait\u2026 I have an idea.\u201d\n \n\n\n\n You\u2019ll get to:\n \n\n\n* Come up with Reel and YouTube ideas\n* Write hooks, scripts, captions and campaign concepts\n* Research trends before everyone gets bored of them\n* **Get in front of the camera and actually create content**\n* **Work on shoots with videographers, editors and designers**\n* **Create content for Instagram, YouTube and Facebook**\n* **Brainstorm ads, creator collaborations and brand campaigns**\n* **Look at analytics and figure out why something worked**\n* **Use AI and creative tools to make ideas happen faster**\n* **Occasionally pitch something completely ridiculous that somehow becomes our best\\-performing content**\n\n\n One Important Thing\n \n**You HAVE to be comfortable in front of the camera.** \n\n\n\n\n**You don\u2019t need 100K followers.** \n\n\n\n\n**You don\u2019t need to be an actor.** \n\n\n\n\n**You don\u2019t need a perfectly curated Instagram profile.** \n\n\n\n\n**But if someone says \u201ccamera rolling\u201d** \n , you shouldn\u2019t disappear from the room.\n \n\n\n You\u2019ll Love This Role If\u2026\n * You genuinely want to become a content creator or marketer.\n* You spend too much time on Instagram and YouTube and call it \u201cresearch.\u201d\n* You instinctively notice good hooks, edits, trends and storytelling.\n* You have ideas and actually want to make them.\n* You want to learn content, branding, social media, advertising, influencer marketing and performance marketing together.\n* You would rather be\n **making the campaign** \n than sitting in a meeting discussing it for three weeks.\n\n\n\n Experience helps.\n \n\n\n\n But\n **energy, creativity, curiosity, communication skills and the hunger to make great content matter more to us.** \n\n\n\n\n**If you\u2019ve been waiting for a job where creating content is actually part of your job\u2026** \n\n\n\n* **this might be it.**","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467503593","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467503593"},{"title":"Marketing Operations Specialist, Asset Management","company":"Northern Trust","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4452228314","source":"linkedin","experience":"3 Yrs","skills":[42,103,106,107,112],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**About Northern Trust**\n As a global leader in innovative wealth management, asset servicing, asset management and banking services, Northern Trust (Nasdaq: NTRS) is proud to guide the world\u2019s most successful individuals, families, corporations and institutions.\n   \n\n  \n\n Since 1889, we have aligned our efforts with our three guiding Principles That Endure: Service, Expertise, and Integrity. Together, they reflect the three cornerstones of business conduct which we strive to instill in our employees, whom we call partners, and to provide to our clients and the communities we serve worldwide.\n   \n\n  \n\n With more than 135 years of financial experience and over 24,000 partners, we serve the world\u2019s most sophisticated clients using leading technology and exceptional service.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Overview Of The Role**\n Northern Trust Asset Management's global marketing strategy is evolving, our team is growing and we\u2019re looking for individuals interested in growing with us. We are seeking passionate, results\\-driven, creative thinkers, with a high attention to detail who value collaboration.\n   \n\n  \n\n Reporting to the Head of Product Marketing Operations, the Marketing Operations Specialist position is a generalist role within our production team in Marketing Operations. The production team establishes and adapts the update cycle process and procedures to create scale and mitigate marketing/business risk. This includes, but is not limited to, creating a cycle framework, implementing regulatory updates, managing collateral updates, and automating deliverables. The team also assists with Seismic, specifically content maintenance and uploads and executing tasks designed to modernize the platform.\n   \n\n  \n\n The Marketing Operations Specialist has primary responsibility for the updating, maintenance and production of our quarterly and annual performance marketing content and materials across print and digital platforms. Secondarily, during off\\-update cycle periods, the Specialist will take on additional efficiency projects.\n   \n\n  \n\n The role will require strong collaboration and partnership within Marketing and across Data Operations and Technology, Product Development and Management, Investments and Client Portfolio Management, Compliance and Legal, and Distribution to establish clear objectives and priorities.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Responsibilities**\n* Complete quarterly/annual update cycle of collateral materials (pitchbooks, profiles, flyers, bios, etc.) including content updates, status reporting, compliance submissions, and being well\\-versed with all data and sources (performance, characteristics, rankings, internal databases, etc.)\n* Create and manage procedures to efficiently and effectively scale content update \\& maintenance, mitigate risk and comply with industry and internal standards\n* Establish and maintain relationships throughout the firm, across Compliance, Technology/Data, Client Portfolio Managers/Portfolio Managers, Distribution, Reporting, and others\n* Implement ad hoc content updates due to organization changes, fund actions, and regulatory rules \\& changes, as established by governing bodies (SEC, FINRA, ASIC, FCA, ESMA, etc.), across various investment offerings, regions, and marketing assets, including coordinating changes to product webpages\n* Review and identify opportunities to use technology to support efficiency and/or automation of marketing content and recurring deliverables, eliminating data dependency, redundancy \\& reduce cycle time\n* Be intellectually curious, gain a knowledge and understanding of our products, as well as continuing to research and learn about Marketing Operations and production advances in the industry\n* Increase productivity by simplifying workflows using data and AI\u2011and automation\\-driven tools\n* Support the overall Marketing Operations team, acting as back\\-up support for other roles and responsibilities within the group as designated\n\n\n**Experience \\& Skills**\n The successful candidate will benefit from having:\n   \n\n  \n\n* 3 years of financial services performance/data update experience preferred\n* Understanding of the investment management industry, familiarity with investment vehicles, marketing constructs, regulatory requirements, and distribution channels preferred\n* Effective collaboration and communication (verbal \\& written) skills\n* Strong attention to detail, organizational skills, with a commitment to quality\n* Ability to prioritize in a fast\\-paced environment\n* Ability to follow established procedures and maintain accurate records\n* Ability to think creatively and outside the box to find to solutions to known problems\n* Demonstrated ability to multi\\-task, \u00adeffectively manage and navigate multiple projects, organize competing objectives and manage deadlines\n* Strong work ethic and professional demeanor\n* Creative and technical abilities across the Microsoft office suite, including Copilot\n\n\n**Working with Us**\n As a Northern Trust partner, you will be part of a flexible and collaborative work culture, which has a strong history of financial strength and stability. Movement within the organization is encouraged, senior leaders are accessible, and you can take pride in working for a company committed to an inclusive workplace and assisting the communities we serve.\n   \n\n  \n\n Philanthropy is deeply rooted in Northern Trust\u2019s history and is an essential element of our culture. Employees around the world give their time and talent to work for the greater good of their communities.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Reasonable Accommodation**\n Northern Trust is committed to working with and providing adjustments to individuals with health conditions and disabilities. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please email our HR Service Center at MyHRHelp@ntrs.com, or alternatively you can discuss your individual requirements with the recruiter you are working with.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About Our Bangalore Office**\n The Northern Trust Bangalore office, established in 2005, is home to over 5,600 employees. In this stunning office space, we offer fantastic amenities which include our Arrival Hub \\- Jungle, the GameZone, and the Employee Experience Zone that appeal to both clients and employees. Learn more.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4452228314","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4452228314"},{"title":"Marketing Intern","company":"Viwidh Foodcraft","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467199429","source":"linkedin","experience":"Intern","skills":[7,107],"is_walkin":false,"description":"Viwidh Foodcraft \\| 3\\-Month Project\\-Based Internship\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\*\\*Location:\\*\\* Bangalore (On\\-Site)\n \n\n\n\n \\*\\*Duration:\\*\\* 3 Months\n \n\n\n\n \\*\\*Type:\\*\\* Project\\-Based Internship\n \n\n\n\n \\*\\*Stipend:\\*\\* As per market standards\n \n\n\n\n \\*\\*Joining:\\*\\* Immediate\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\#\\#\\# About Roti Kulcha Naan\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Roti Kulcha Naan is a growing food brand focused on serving great North Indian breads and food in a quick\\-service format.\n \n\n\n\n We\u2019re looking for energetic, curious and creative \\*\\*Marketing Interns\\*\\* who want to get hands\\-on experience building marketing for a real consumer brand.\n \n\n\n\n This is not a typical internship where you'll spend three months making presentations and watching from the sidelines.\n \n\n\n\n You\u2019ll be involved in \\*\\*coming up with ideas, executing them, testing what works and measuring the results.\\*\\*\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\#\\#\\# What You'll Work On\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Depending on your strengths and interests, you could work on projects across:\n \n\n\n\n \\*\\*Social Media \\& Content\n \n\n\n\n \\* Plan and execute Instagram content and Reels\n \n\n\n\n \\* Come up with creative content ideas around food, customers and the brand\n \n\n\n\n \\* Help create photos and videos at our outlets\n \n\n\n\n \\* Experiment with different content formats and understand what performs\n \n\n\n\n \\* Build and maintain a content calendar\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\*\\*Local Store Marketing\n \n\n\n\n \\* Identify marketing opportunities around our outlets\n \n\n\n\n \\* Plan campaigns targeting nearby colleges, offices, apartments and communities\n \n\n\n\n \\* Explore partnerships with local businesses and communities\n \n\n\n\n \\* Come up with ideas to increase awareness and footfall\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\*\\*Customer Growth\n \n\n\n\n \\* Develop ideas to bring in new customers\n \n\n\n\n \\* Find ways to increase repeat orders\n \n\n\n\n \\* Work on referral, loyalty and promotional campaigns\n \n\n\n\n \\* Explore WhatsApp and other customer engagement channels\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\*\\*Marketing Experiments\n \n\n\n\n \\* Identify a problem or opportunity\n \n\n\n\n \\* Come up with a campaign or experiment\n \n\n\n\n \\* Execute it with the team\n \n\n\n\n \\* Measure the results\n \n\n\n\n \\* Figure out what worked and what didn't\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\*\\*Competitor \\& Market Research\n \n\n\n\n \\* Study other food and QSR brands\n \n\n\n\n \\* Track their campaigns, offers and content\n \n\n\n\n \\* Identify interesting ideas that RKN can learn from or test\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\#\\#\\# What We're Looking For\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n You don't need to have previous marketing experience.\n \n\n\n\n We care more about \\*\\*how you think and how much initiative you take.\\*\\*\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n You'd be a great fit if you:\n \n\n\n\n \\* Are creative and constantly coming up with ideas\n \n\n\n\n \\* Understand Instagram, Reels and social media culture\n \n\n\n\n \\* Enjoy creating content or experimenting with new formats\n \n\n\n\n \\* Communicate well and aren't afraid to approach people\n \n\n\n\n \\* Are curious about why customers behave the way they do\n \n\n\n\n \\* Can take an idea from concept to execution\n \n\n\n\n \\* Are comfortable working in a fast\\-moving, hands\\-on environment\n \n\n\n\n \\* Are willing to go beyond your assigned task when you see something that can be improved\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\*\\*Students pursuing Marketing, Business, Media, Design, Communications or similar fields are welcome to apply.\\*\\*\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n But your degree matters less to us than your \\*\\*ability, curiosity and attitude.\\*\\*\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\#\\#\\# What You'll Get\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\* Hands\\-on experience working with a real consumer/food brand\n \n\n\n\n \\* Ownership of actual marketing projects\n \n\n\n\n \\* Opportunity to see your ideas go from concept to execution\n \n\n\n\n \\* Exposure to social media, local marketing, customer acquisition and brand building\n \n\n\n\n \\* Regular feedback and mentorship\n \n\n\n\n \\* A portfolio of real projects and campaigns you can showcase\n \n\n\n\n \\* Certificate of internship on successful completion\n \n\n\n\n \\* \\*\\*Performance\\-based opportunity for continued work with Roti Kulcha Naan\\*\\*\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\#\\#\\# What Success Looks Like\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n By the end of the internship, you shouldn't just be able to say:\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\> \"I interned at bla bla bla.\"\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n You should be able to say:\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\> \"I ran these campaigns, created this content, tested these ideas and generated these results.\"\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n That's what we're looking for.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\#\\#\\# How to Apply\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Send us:\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \\*\\*1\\. Your resume\\*\\*\n \n\n\n\n \\*\\*2\\. A short introduction about yourself\\*\\*\n \n\n\n\n \\*\\*3\\. One marketing idea you'd like our brand to try\\*\\*\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n No fancy cover letter required.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467199429","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467199429"},{"title":"Content and Social Media Marketing Internship in Bangalore (Hybrid)","company":"SuperLiving","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468310798","source":"linkedin","experience":"Intern","is_walkin":false,"description":"**Selected Intern's Day\\-to\\-day Responsibilities Include**\n* Run a weekly scout across Meta Ad Library, Reels, YouTube Shorts and Instagram for hooks, formats and claims working in weight loss, skin, hair, stress, acidity, sugar and sexual wellness\\- eight categories, each with its own audience.\n* Write up what you find as a concept, not a screenshot: what the hook is, why it works, which of our categories it transfers to, and what breaks if we copy it straight.\n* Build the asset yourself in our internal tool\\- basic prompting; iterate until the output is usable. You don't need to be a prompt engineer; you need to be stubborn about output quality.\n* Ship a set volume of testable concepts every week into our CPI Testing campaigns, and read back which of yours survived to scaling.\n\n\n About Company: Welcome to SuperLiving: India's most trusted AI\\-powered lifestyle companion! SuperLiving is uniquely designed for the lifestyle needs of Indian families. Powered by cutting\\-edge AI and created by experts, SuperLiving offers personalized wellness courses, daily guidance, expert support, personal coaches and engaging community experiences specifically tailored for Bharat. Download SuperLiving now and step into a healthier, happier life, effortlessly!","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468310798","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468310798"},{"title":"Content Marketing Intern","company":"21K School","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467512291","source":"linkedin","experience":"2 Yrs","skills":[103,104,107,116,117],"is_walkin":false,"description":"About 21K School\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n 21K School is Asia\u2019s leading online school, delivering world\\-class, personalised education to learners across 70\\+ countries.\n \n\n\n\n We are building the future of schooling \u2014 one that is borderless, flexible, and learner\\-centric. Our model combines academic excellence, technology, and strong parent engagement to create a scalable and future\\-ready learning ecosystem.\n \n\n\n\n As we continue to scale, building facilitator capability and ensuring consistent pedagogical excellence across grades and curricula is a key strategic priority.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n About The Role\n \n\n\n* We are looking for a creative and proactive Social Media \\& Content Intern who will support our leadership\u2019s presence on social platforms (especially LinkedIn), help create newsletters, and manage engaging content across Instagram and other channels. You will work closely with the marketing and communications teams to build and strengthen our online voice with clarity, creativity, and strategic intent.Key ResponsibilitiesCreate compelling and professional content for LinkedIn, Instagram, newsletters, and other platforms\n* Work with senior leadership to communicate ideas, insights, and thought leadership content in written and visual formats\n* Support content ideation, scheduling, posting, and basic performance tracking\n* Assist in growing engagement and community interaction with consistent, brand\\-aligned posts\n* Collaborate with the design and marketing teams for creative assets\n* Maintain content calendars and help with execution of campaigns and newsletters\n* What We\u2019re Looking ForFreshers passionate about social media, content, and storytelling (1\u20132 yrs experience is also fine)\n* Strong written communication and creative thinking skills\n* Portfolio showcasing social media work (LinkedIn, Instagram, newsletters, blogs, content series, campaigns) \u2014 required\n* Familiarity with LinkedIn content and audience dynamics\n* Basic experience with design or content tools (Canva, Figma, CapCut, video editing tools) is a plus\n* Ability to work onsite in Bengaluru with your own laptop.\n* What You\u2019ll GainReal\\-world experience managing professional brand and leadership content\n* Strong exposure to content strategy and social media engagement\n* Mentorship and feedback from experienced marketing and leadership teams\n* A portfolio that reflects versatile content creation skills\n* Stipend and Certification","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467512291","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467512291"},{"title":"Senior Events Marketing Specialist","company":"Xoxoday","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467129718","source":"linkedin","experience":"6 Yrs","skills":[103,105,107],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**About This Role**\n We\u2019re looking for a senior events marketing specialist to help build awareness and demand for Xoxoday across global markets through events and webinars. This role exists to create meaningful engagement with our target personas and translate that engagement into qualified pipeline.\n   \n\n  \n\n You\u2019ll work closely with sales, product, and the broader marketing team to plan and execute field campaigns that align with our messaging and business priorities. This is an execution\\-focused role with room to experiment, learn, and improve outcomes over time.\n   \n\n  \n\n**What You\u2019ll Do**\n**Field Events \\& Webinars**\n* Plan and execute field events and webinars aligned to campaign themes\n* Identify and manage vendors, negotiate contracts, and coordinate logistics\n* Drive end\\-to\\-end event execution from concept to post\\-event follow\\-up\n\n\n**Campaign Activation**\n* Design pre\\-event and post\\-event campaigns to generate and nurture leads\n* Partner with content and digital teams to promote events across channels\n* Develop messaging tailored to target personas and regional context\n\n\n**Cross\\-Functional Collaboration**\n* Partner with sales to align on target accounts and follow\\-up strategy\n* Work with product and marketing teams to ensure campaign relevance\n* Coordinate with agencies and external partners as required\n\n\n**Performance \\& Reporting**\n* Track event and webinar performance\n* Measure pipeline contribution and overall return on event investments\n* Share insights and recommend improvements for future campaigns\n\n\n**What We\u2019re Looking For**\n 1\\.3\u20136 years of experience in offline and digital events marketing, preferably in a SaaS environment\n   \n\n  \n\n* Experience supporting marketing initiatives across international markets\n* Strong collaboration skills across sales, product, analytics, and content teams\n* Clear communication and negotiation skills\n* Ability to manage multiple workstreams with attention to detail\n\n\n**Nice to Have**\n* Exposure to US or European markets in a similar role\n\n\n**What Makes You a Strong Fit**\n* Approach marketing with curiosity and a willingness to experiment\n* Take ownership of execution and follow through on deliverables\n* Communicate clearly across teams and stakeholders\n* Stay organized while managing multiple timelines\n\n\n**Why This Role Matters**\n Events and webinars play a critical role in how we build trust, educate buyers, and create demand. This role directly supports revenue growth by creating structured, measurable engagement with our target audience.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Why Join Us**\n* Work on global campaigns across diverse markets\n* Collaborate with cross\\-functional teams in a fast\\-paced environment\n* Gain hands\\-on exposure to end\\-to\\-end field marketing\n* Contribute to products used by global clients\n* Grow your marketing skills through practical ownership and execution","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467129718","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467129718"},{"title":"Marketing","company":"Caramelo Studio","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468363917","source":"linkedin","experience":"Intern","skills":[3,105],"is_walkin":false,"description":"YOUR\n **NEXT CREATIVE CHAPTER COULD START TOMORROW.** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Some people don\u2019t just watch stories.\n \n\n\n\n They\n **sell them. Shoot them. Edit them. Animate them. Bring them to life.** \n\n\n\n\n At\n **Caramelo Studio, Bangalore** \n , we\u2019re looking for people who want to do exactly that.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n We\u2019re opening opportunities for:\n \n\n\n* Sales\n **Intern\u2014Turn** \n conversations into opportunities.\n* Videographer\n **\\& Editor** \n \u2014 Capture moments. Create stories.\n* Animator\u2014Make ideas move.\n* **Cinematographer\u2014Turn** \n frames into experiences.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n And yes\u2026\n **We want to meet YOU, not just your resume.** \n\n\n\n\n \ud83d\udccd\n **Bangalore \\| Lollypop Office** \n\n\n\n\n \ud83e\udd1d\n **Interview Mode: FACE\\-TO\\-FACE** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Office Address:** \n\n\n\n\n \\#69, KMJ Atelier, Besides DHL Express,\n