, and data interpretation.\n* Leverage SQL, Looker, Power BI, or other BI tools for deeper analysis where required.\n* Continuously test and implement new campaign strategies, audiences, creatives, and bidding approaches.\n\n\n\n Required Skills \\& Qualifications\n \n\n\n* **2\u20134 years of experience** \n in Performance Marketing / Digital Marketing.\n* Strong hands\\-on experience with\n **Meta Ads** \n , preferably managing campaigns at significant scale.\n* Strong analytical and problem\\-solving skills with the ability to work with raw data.\n* Good understanding of\n **campaign structure, bidding, audience targeting, attribution, and conversion funnels** \n .\n* Strong proficiency in\n **Excel / Google Sheets** \n .\n* Ability to independently diagnose campaign performance issues and identify actionable solutions.\n* Strong communication and cross\\-functional collaboration skills.\n\n\n\n Good to Have\n \n\n\n* **Engineering background** \n preferred.\n* Experience with\n **CAPI, Advantage\\+, and tROAS bidding** \n .\n* Knowledge of\n **SQL, Looker, Power BI** \n , or similar BI tools.\n* Experience in large\\-scale lead generation or consumer\\-facing performance marketing.\n* Exposure to experimentation, A/B testing, and funnel optimization.\n\n\n\n Ideal Candidate\n \n\n\n\n We are looking for someone who goes beyond simply monitoring dashboards \u2014 someone who is\n **curious, analytical, and proactive** \n , and enjoys digging into data to understand\n *why* \n performance is changing and what can be done to improve it.\n \n\n\n\n**Location:** \n Bangalore\n \n\n\n\n**Experience:** \n 2\u20134 Years\n \n\n\n\n**Reporting:** \n Growth \\& Performance Marketing Leadership","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467174535","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467174535"},{"title":"PPC Specialist","company":"Munim - Accounting, Billing & GST Software","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466225180","source":"linkedin","experience":"6 Yrs","skills":[105,107,108,109,112],"is_walkin":false,"description":"3 \\- 6 Years\n   \n\n  \n\n Bengaluru, Surat\n   \n\n  \n\n Full\\-Time\n   \n\n  \n\n**Job Description**\n We are looking for a highly experienced PPC Specialist to manage paid campaigns for SaaS products for both domestic and international markets. The role is suitable for a product\\-based or service\\-based company working with B2B or B2C SaaS.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Roles \\& Responsibilities**\n* Plan, create and manage PPC campaigns for SaaS products across Google Ads, Meta Ads, E\\-mail Marketing, LinkedIn Ads, etc.\n* Run campaigns targeted to both Indian and international audiences (geo targeting, time zones, currencies where required).\n* Conduct keyword research, audience targeting and competitor analysis for multiple markets.\n* Create and test ad copies, landing pages and extensions to improve CTR and conversion rate.\n* Monitor daily performance of campaigns and optimize for CPL, CAC and ROAS.\n* Set up and track conversions using Google Analytics, Tag Manager, and other tools.\n* Prepare weekly and monthly performance reports with insights and recommendations.\n* Collaborate with sales, marketing and product teams to align campaigns with business goals.\n\n\n**Qualification and Requirement**\n* 3\\+ years of strong experience in PPC / Performance Marketing.\n* Proven experience running campaigns for SaaS products (product or service company, domestic and/or international).\n* Excellent knowledge of Google Ads; experience with LinkedIn Ads and remarketing is preferred.\n* Strong knowledge of LinkedIn Recruiter, Boolean search techniques, and social recruiting tools.\n* Data\\-driven mindset with strong analytical and reporting skills.\n\n\n**Required Skills**\n Google Ads Google Tag Manager Bid strategy \\& budget optimization Meta Ads Keyword research \\& intent mapping Ad copywriting Audience targeting \\& remarketing Google Analytics Campaign structure \\& account organization A/B testing\n   \n\n  \n\n Share with someone awesome\n   \n\n  \n\n View all job openings","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466225180","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466225180"},{"title":"Performance Manager","company":"Bolas Agro Private Limited","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468361801","source":"linkedin","experience":"Manager","skills":[101,104,107],"is_walkin":false,"description":"* Lead the in\\-house channel performance team \u2014 the existing Performance Marketing \u2013 Quick Commerce and the new Performance Marketing \u2013 E\\-commerce report in.\n* Manage the Shizz relationship for Meta as an interim arrangement \u2014 set targets, review performance, hold them accountable \u2014 and plan and execute the transition to an in\\-house Meta / YouTube team, then hire and lead it.\n* Build the performance function: structure, tooling, dashboards and the hiring roadmap as spends scale.\n\n\n\n**IN\\-CHANNEL / RETAIL MEDIA** \n\n\n\n* Own overall retail\\-media strategy and blended ROAS / TACOS across qcom (Blinkit, Zepto, Instamart) and marketplace (Amazon, Flipkart), setting the framework the channel performance team executes against.\n* Partner with the qcom and marketplace KAMs so ad investment maps to assortment, availability and margin \u2014 no spending behind OOS or low\\-margin SKUs.\n\n\n\n**BRAND\\-SIDE DIGITAL \u2014 META / YOUTUBE / GOOGLE** \n\n\n\n* Own the full\\-funnel paid strategy on Meta, YouTube, Google Search / Shopping and programmatic \u2014 acquisition, retargeting and D2C growth.\n* Drive creative testing at scale with the brand team \u2014 hooks, formats, UGC \u2014 and build a feedback loop between creative and performance.\n* Own audience, measurement and attribution \u2014 pixels, events, MMM / incrementality thinking \u2014 so decisions rest on real marginal return, not last\\-click vanity.\n\n\n\n**CROSS\\-CUTTING** \n\n\n\n* Own the performance budget and its allocation across channels; report blended CAC, ROAS, contribution and payback to leadership.\n* Set the measurement and reporting standard across all paid channels (bring in the Dcluttr data layer where useful).","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468361801","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468361801"},{"title":"Content Strategist","company":"CeeQ","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468357997","source":"linkedin","experience":"5 Yrs","skills":[103,107],"is_walkin":false,"description":"We seek a content strategist for a personal care D2C brand in Bengaluru.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Job Responsibilities** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Performance \\& Digital Creative\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Develop copy and creative ideas for Meta and Google performance campaigns.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Understand different consumer personas, pain points and stages of awareness to build relevant communication.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Write strong hooks, headlines, propositions, benefit\\-led copy and CTAs built to drive action.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Think beyond copy execution and contribute creative concepts and angles for performance ads.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Learn from creative performance and use those insights to develop stronger iterations and new ideas.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Website \\& Landing Pages\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Write and structure copy for landing pages, product pages, category pages and other website journeys.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Understand how information, persuasion and proof need to build as a consumer moves through a page.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Turn product features into clear, compelling consumer benefits.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Write with conversion, hierarchy and user intent in mind.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Social, Campaigns \\& Brand\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Contribute ideas and copy for social media, campaigns, launches and cultural moments.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Participate in creative brainstorming for shoots, content formats and larger brand ideas.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Write across formats including statics, carousels, reels, scripts, captions and campaign communication.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Adapt Mahina\u2019s voice across channels while keeping the brand recognisable and consistent.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Job Qualifications** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n \u25cf 1\u20135 years of experience in content strategy, content marketing, or brand writing roles\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Proven ability to lead cross\\-functional content projects end\\-to\\-end\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Strong understanding of both formats (ads, videos, carousels, banners, blogs) and channels (Meta, LinkedIn, email, website, marketplaces, Google Ads, etc.)\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Sharp copy instincts \\+ content intuition that balances brand and performance\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Exceptional spoken and written English, with a basic understanding of visual communication.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468357997","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468357997"},{"title":"Associate, Paid Social","company":"Assembly Global","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468214474","source":"linkedin","skills":[30],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**About Us**\n At Assembly, we help brands find the change to fuel business growth. We are an award\\-winning global brand performance agency, home to 1,600 talented people across 25 offices globally. We create unique data, technology and media solutions that enable faster and smarter problem solving and an inspired, collaborative workplace culture.\n   \n\n  \n\n At Assembly we embody three core values: Show Up \\- actively contribute to a space of personal and collective growth; Make Change \\- embrace obstacles as opportunities, taking intentional steps to drive positive change; and Win Well \\- approach success with integrity, responsibility, and a commitment to collaboration, understanding that the journey is as important as the destination. Together, we create an environment that fosters continuous learning, adaptability, and a shared passion for making a meaningful impact.\n   \n\n  \n\n We stay ahead of what\u2019s next, providing fresh insights to spark new ideas. We\u2019re a trusted partner to our clients, working behind the scenes to bring imagination, depth, and clarity to their biggest challenges\u2014in entertainment, technology, lifestyle, sports, and gaming. Together, we create with confidence\n   \n\n  \n\n**Overview**\n The\u202f Paid Social Specialist \u202fwould be responsible for managing advertising campaigns for clients in global markets , on various Paid Social platforms like, Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Pinterest , and Snap to name a few. The individual will be responsible for planning, building, optimizing campaigns, and analyze performance based on client objectives . He/she may eventually also manage a team based on his/her capabilities and performance.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Responsibilities**\n* Manage paid social campaigns based on the agreed\\-upon strategic direction provided by the US team members.\n* Ensure campaign setup and delivery is aligned with the tactical plan and offer strategic and tactical recommendations to help shape future planning.\n* Optimize media campaigns towards the target KPIs within various advertising platforms, including but not limited to:\n* Facebook Ads Manager\n* Instagram Ads\n* LinkedIn Advertising Products\n* Twitter\n* Pinterest\n* Snap\n* Support the development of best practices in ad trafficking through Double C lick Campaign Manager (DCM) for all display and paid social campaigns.\n\n\n**Required Skills**\n* Desired Experience \\- 3 \\+ years of experience in managing Paid Social campaigns\n* Experience in setting up and optimizing campaigns on social media platforms like Facebook, LinkedIn, Instagram, Pinterest, Snap, and Twitter\n\n\n**Desired Skills**\n* Experience on Xing, Smartly, 4C, and Sprinklr\n* DSPs and programmatic platforms\n* Creative Studio, DV360, and TTD\n\n\n**Benefits**\n* Annual Leave in number of 15 allotted to all employees beginning of every calendar year.\n* Sick Leave in number of 12 is allotted effective DOJ and beginning of ever calendar year.\n* Other Leaves\\-Maternity Leave \\& Paternity Leaves, Birthday Leave Entitlement\n* Dedicated L\\&D Budget for all Teams to upskill \\& get certified\n* All employees are entitled for Group Personal Accident Cover \\& Life Cover Insurance.\n* Insurance coverage for the entire family (Employee \\+ up to 7 dependents \\- Self, Spouse, up to 4 children, and Parents)\n* Monthly Cross Team Lunch\n* Rewards and Recognition program\\-Employee of the month, Star Performer, Tenure Celebration \\& many more\n\n\n**Equal Opportunities**\n Assembly is an advocate for equal opportunity in the workplace. We are committed to ensuring equal opportunities regardless of race, colour, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability and gender identity. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements. If you have a disability or special need that requires accommodation, please let us know.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Social and Environmental Responsibility**\n At Assembly, we have a responsibility to bring impact into our every day. This means we must always look for ways in which to be conscious citizens in our roles to support society and environmental sustainability. We encourage employees to; be a conscious citizen by actively participating in our organisation's sustainability efforts, help us promote environmentally friendly practices within the workplace, collaborate with community organisations and stakeholders to support initiatives aligned with our company's values, participate in volunteer activities that benefit the community. Employees are also encouraged to make suggestions and evaluate our business practices to identify areas for improvement in social and environmental performance. Employees at Assembly demonstrate commitment to sustainability and inclusivity in their actions and behaviors.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468214474","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468214474"},{"title":"Executive | Sr Executive | Manager - Media Planning","company":"WPP Media","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468361864","source":"linkedin","experience":"4 Yrs","skills":[33,103,104,107],"is_walkin":false,"description":"****About WPP Media****\n WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world\u2019s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world\\-class partnerships \u2013 all united by our\u202fpioneering\u202fagentic marketing platform, WPP Open \u2013 we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth.\n   \n\n  \n\n WPP Media is WPP's AI\\-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.\n   \n\n  \n\n For more information, visit wppmedia.com.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Executive \\| Sr Executive \\| Manager \u2013 Implementation Planning, GOC**\n****About WPP Media****\n WPP is the creative transformation company. We use the power of creativity to build better futures for our people, planet, clients and communities. For more information, visit wpp.com.\n   \n\n  \n\n WPP Media is WPP\u2019s global media collective. In a world where media is everywhere and in everything, we bring the best platform, people, and partners together to create limitless opportunities for growth. For more information, visit wppmedia.com\n   \n\n  \n\n At WPP Media, We Believe In The Power Of Our Culture And Our People. It\u2019s What Elevates Us To Deliver Exceptional Experiences For Both Our Clients And Each Other. In This Role It Will Be Critical To Embrace WPP \\& WPP Media\u2019s Shared Core Values:\n   \n\n  \n\n* Be Extraordinary by Leading Collectively to Inspire transformational Creativity.\n* Create an Open environment by Balancing People and Client Experiences by Cultivating Trust.\n* Lead Optimistically by Championing Growth and Development to Mobilize the Enterprise.\n\n\n****Role Summary And Impact****\n As part of the\n **Global Operations Centre (GOC)** \n , you will work closely with teams across the United States, Europe, and Asia to deliver high\\-impact solutions in a collaborative, multicultural environment. We are looking for a Senior Executive \u2013 Implementation Planning who will:\n   \n\n  \n\n* Develop strong relationships with Client Servicing and Activation teams to facilitate flawless execution of plans.\n* Communicate effectively across all levels of the team and across all practices.\n* Support Media Planning Managers to ensure the smooth delivery of campaigns and their performance against agreed outcomes.\n* Conduct research and compile data to guide and support planning and optimization recommendations.\n* Compile and validate creative specs. Collaborate with creative agency partners to ensure deadlines are met.\n* Collaborate with Activation teams to complete the detail of the plan in Olive.\n* Create trafficking sheet templates and collaborate with Ad Operations through campaign launch.\n* Prepare data for reporting and analysis.\n* Support the team in making optimisation recommendations.\n* Assist in the management of testing plans for assigned campaigns.\n* Contribute to internal case studies for the sharing of learning and best practice.\n* Meet with vendors and attend presentations to build knowledge of the media landscape\n\n\n****Skills And Experience****\n* Media Planning are experts on the paid media landscape and how consumers interact with it. We architect and steward holistic media plans throughout their lifecycle, owning the creation of overall plans, cross\\-channel budget allocation, in\\-flight cross\\-channel optimization \\& reporting and post\\-campaign analysis. We are our clients\u2019 key contacts for a unified view across all aspects of their campaigns, narrating the story of the campaign from planning recommendation through to PCA.\n* Bachelor's degree in marketing, advertising, business, or a related field.\n* 2\\-4 years of B2B program marketing experience, preferably in the technology field; enterprise infrastructure software marketing experience is a huge plus\n* In\\-depth knowledge of media planning principles, techniques, and best practices across various channels (digital \\& social)\n* Familiarity with media buying, negotiation, and contract management.\n* Strong analytical skills and ability to interpret data and metrics to make data\\-driven decisions.\n* Proficiency in using media planning and tracking tools (Marketo, Convertr or Data Studio is a plus)\n* Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively with cross\\-functional teams.\n* Computer literate with good skills in all basic Office programs (including Excel)\n* Creative thinking and problem\\-solving abilities.\n* A passion for everything media and advertising, coupled with a continued desire to expand your knowledge\n\n\n****Life At WPP Media \\& Benefits****\n Our passion for shaping the next era of media includes investing in our employees to help them do their best work, and we\u2019re just as committed to employee growth as we are to responsible media investment. WPP Media employees can tap into the global WPP Media \\& WPP networks to pursue their passions, grow their networks, and learn at the cutting edge of marketing and advertising. We have a variety of employee resource groups and host frequent in\\-office events showcasing team wins, sharing thought leadership, and celebrating holidays and milestone events. Our benefits include access to internal learning platforms, certifications, and training sessions, life insurance, wellness programs, significant paid time off, preferential partner discounts, employee mental health awareness day, and more.\n   \n\n  \n\n Research shows that candidates from underrepresented backgrounds often don't apply for roles if they don't meet all the criteria.\u202fAt WPP Media, we strongly encourage you to apply if you\u2019re interested, we'd love to know how you can positively impact our team with your experience!\n   \n\n  \n\n As an Equal Opportunities Employer, we believe that diversity is vital and positively influences the environment in which we operate. We are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive work environment that is free of discrimination, harassment or bullying. Race, colour, ancestry, religion, gender, gender identity, national origin, sexual orientation, age, marital status or disability status have no bearing on our hiring decisions, and we encourage all applicants.\n   \n\n  \n\n We view everyone as an individual and we understand that inclusion is more than just diversity \u2013 it\u2019s about belonging. We celebrate the fact that everyone is unique and that\u2019s what makes us so good at what we do. We pride ourselves on being a company that embraces difference and truly represents the global clients we work with.\n   \n\n  \n\n We believe the best work happens when we're together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That's why we\u2019ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.\n   \n\n  \n\n Please read our Privacy Notice (\n **https://www.wppmedia.com/pages/privacy\\-policy** \n ) for more information on how we process the information you provide.\n   \n\n  \n\n While we appreciate all applications received, only those candidates selected for an interview will be contacted.\n   \n\n  \n\n Please read our Privacy Notice for more information on how we process the information you provide.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468361864","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468361864"},{"title":"SBS -Assistant Brand Manager, India Consumables","company":"Amazon","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4459172693","source":"linkedin","experience":"Manager","skills":[12,24,105,107,108,112],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**Description**\n Join our Strategic Brand Services team at Amazon India where you'll partner with top\\-tier brands to accelerate their growth on Amazon. You'll drive strategic initiatives across selection expansion, marketing effectiveness, and inventory optimization while collaborating with cross\\-functional teams to implement data\\-driven solutions that enhance customer experience.\n   \n\n  \n\n Key job responsibilities\n   \n\n  \n\n* Lead strategic planning and execution of selection expansion initiatives by analyzing market trends and identifying growth opportunities\n* Create and implement marketing strategies to drive brand awareness and customer engagement on Amazon\n* Develop and maintain strong partnerships with brands to optimize their catalog quality and product content\n* Analyze performance metrics and provide actionable recommendations to improve brand performance\n* Collaborate with internal teams to ensure product availability and supply chain efficiency\n* Drive adoption of Amazon programs and tools to maximize brand growth potential\n\n\n A day in the life\n   \n\n  \n\n You'll start your day reviewing key performance metrics for your brand portfolio, followed by strategy sessions with brand partners. Throughout the day, you'll collaborate with marketing, catalog, and operations teams to drive improvements across various business levers. You'll analyze data to identify growth opportunities and develop action plans to capitalize on them\n   \n\n  \n\n**About The Team**\n Strategic Brand Services is a new initiative at Amazon India focused on providing dedicated support to premium brands. Our team combines analytical rigor with creative problem\\-solving to help brands achieve their full potential on Amazon.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Basic Qualifications**\n* 2\\+ years of account management, project or program management or buying experience\n* Bachelor's degree\n* Experience using analytical specific tools such as Google Analytics, SQL or HTML\n\n\n**Preferred Qualifications**\n* Experience in process improvement\n* Experience managing large amounts of data\n\n\n Our inclusive culture empowers Amazonians to deliver the best results for our customers. If you have a disability and need a workplace accommodation or adjustment during the application and hiring process, including support for the interview or onboarding process, please visit https://amazon.jobs/content/en/how\\-we\\-hire/accommodations for more information. If the country/region you\u2019re applying in isn\u2019t listed, please contact your Recruiting Partner.\n   \n\n  \n\n  \n\n**Company** \n \\- ASSPL \\- Karnataka\n   \n\n  \n\n Job ID: A10515200","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4459172693","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4459172693"},{"title":"Associate Director - Growth & Retention","company":"Snapmint","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468203601","source":"linkedin","experience":"Manager","skills":[1,12,29,104],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**About Snapmint:** \n\n\n\n\n India\u2019s booming consumer market has over 300 million credit\\-eligible consumers, yet only 35million actively use credit cards. At Snapmint, we are building a better alternative to credit cards that lets consumers buy now and pay later for a wide variety of products, be it shoes, clothes, fashion accessories, clothes or mobile phones. We firmly believe that an enduring financial services business must be built on the bedrock of providing honest, transparent and fair terms.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Founded in 2017, today we are the leading online zero\\-cost EMI provider in India. We have served over 10M consumers across 2,200 cities and are doubling year on year. Our founders are serial entrepreneurs and alumni of IIT Bombay and ISB with over two decades of experience across leading organizations like Swiggy, Oyo, Maruti Suzuki and ZS Associates before successfully scaling and exiting businesses in patent analytics, ad\\-tech and bank\\-tech software services.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Role Overview** \n\n\n\n\n As Senior Manager / Associate Director \u2013 Growth \\& Retention, you will own the full lifecycle P\\&L\u2014from activation to repeat behaviour to reactivation\u2014and lead a multidisciplinary team of 12\u201315 across analytics, CRM, campaign operations, personalisation, and rewards. This is a function\\-head role. You will set strategy, manage a significant incentive budget, and represent Growth \\& Retention in leadership forums.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Responsibilities** \n\n\n\n\n \u25cf Full Lifecycle P\\&L: CLTV, contribution margin, incentive budget allocation, and ROAS across all customer segments and product lines.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Activation: Turn new users (especially checkout\\-origin) into first\\-time transactors on Snapmint; drive app adoption and reduce time\\-to\\-first\\-purchase.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Deepening Engagement: Build the repeat flywheel\u2014cross\\-sell across marketplace, vouchers, personal loans, and recharges; increase multi\\-product adoption.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Retention \\& Reactivation: Prolong active lifespan, predict and reduce churn, run winback campaigns with documented payback periods.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Rewards \\& Loyalty: Oversee the rewards programme as an integrated lifecycle lever\u2014merchant partnerships, unit economics, and programme ROI.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Team \\& Organisational Leadership: Build, mentor, and scale a high\\-performing team; set quarterly priorities; be the executive stakeholder for the CRM/engagement tech stack\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Qualifications:** \n\n\n\n\n \u25cf 7\\+ years of experience, with 4\\+ years in lifecycle/CRM/growth at a consumer internet or fintech company.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf 3\\+ years of people management\u2014you\u2019ve led and developed teams during high\\-growth phases.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Proven P\\&L ownership\u2014you\u2019ve been accountable for a lifecycle or retention budget and its economic outcomes, not just engagement metrics.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Strong analytical foundation: SQL, Python, CLTV/RFM modelling, A/B testing, and cohort economics.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Hands\\-on familiarity with CRM platforms (CleverTap, MoEngage, or similar) and multi\\-channel campaign design (push, WhatsApp, SMS, email, IVR).\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Exposure to rewards or loyalty programme mechanics is a strong plus.\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf A leader who sets the agenda, makes decisions with margin and payback in mind, and drives cross\\-functional influence with Product, Credit, and Data Science.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468203601","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468203601"},{"title":"Assistant Manager- Events","company":"Swiggy","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466843988","source":"linkedin","experience":"2 Yrs","skills":[12,25,33,44,107],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**About Swiggy**\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Swiggy is India\u2019s leading on\\-demand delivery platform with a tech\\-first approach to logistics and a solution\\-first approach to consumer demands. With a presence in 500\\+ cities across India, partnerships with hundreds of thousands of restaurants, an employee base of over 5000, a 2 lakh\\+ strong independent fleet of Delivery Executives, we deliver unparalleled convenience driven by continuous innovation. Built on the back of robust ML technology and fueled by terabytes of data processed every day, Swiggy offers a fast, seamless and reliable delivery experience for millions of customers across India.\n \n\n\n\n From starting out as a hyperlocal food delivery service in 2014, to becoming India\u2019s leading on\\-demand convenience platform today, our capabilities result not only in lightning\\-fast delivery for customers, but also in a productive and fulfilling experience for our employees.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Events Team Overview** \n \\- The Events team is a crucial team within the Revenue \\& Growth function which manages and controls all Events on the Food Delivery BU\u2019s calendar. This includes planning for future events, executing current events and performing analysis of past events to learn from Hits/ Misses and incorporate into future events.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n This role offers the opportunity to do (a) work on building events which are consumer backward (elevating needs, build new use\\-cases) and engaging and (b) data deep\\-dive into consumer trends to identifying new opportunities/events and (c) manage multi\\-objective problems (growth/ consumer delight/ monetization) and also (d) get things done by coordinating with multiple stakeholders. The program is responsible for overall planning \\& execution of high quality events to drive app\\-traffic, move consideration to Swiggy and deliver Order\\-volume goals.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n At Swiggy, we take pride in the impact we create in millions of people\u2019s lives. We value honesty, ownership and a keep\\-pushing boundaries attitude. We promise you\u2019ll be challenged daily with better and interesting problems.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Key Responsibilities \\-** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n 1\\. Plan, strategize, anchor and execute all marketing events for the Food BU on the platform\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n 2\\. Use AI to analyse user behaviour, ordering patterns, cuisine/category trends, regional nuances and seasonality to build relevant event strategies.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n 3\n \n . Stakeholder Management \\& Cross Functional Collaboration :\n \n Solve complex cross\\-functional business problems \\- Work closely with Product, Business, Design, Category, Supply, Monetisation and Marketing teams to identify levers, evaluate trade\\-offs and unlock event growth.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n 3\\.\n \n Performance Tracking, Reporting \\& Optimization\n \n : Establish clear success metrics and measurement frameworks for every initiative; identify drivers and leakages, and optimize interventions in real time.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n 4\\.\n \n Business insighting\n \n : Drive structured reporting and insighting with stakeholders \\& leaders, identify growth opportunities, evaluate initiative effectiveness and enable faster, data\\-backed decision\\-making.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Desirable Skills \\-** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* Undergrad with \\~2 years of high\\-paced experience in consulting/ start ups / ecommerce\n* Sound analytical reasoning \\& abilities\n* Competent in SQL, Google Sheets and MS Excel along with an ability to pick up new tools as required\n* Strong understanding of\n **business metrics and growth funnels** \n , including traffic, conversion, retention and incremental impact.\n* Experience with\n **experimentation, performance measurement and hypothesis\\-driven problem solving** \n would be an advantage.\n* Understand tech and product building (would be an added advantage)\n* Very high on consumer backward thinking\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by the law.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466843988","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466843988"},{"title":"Content Marketer","company":"Murf AI","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466265305","source":"linkedin","skills":[9,24,104,107,108],"is_walkin":false,"description":"At Murf AI, we are simplifying voice integration and creation for builders and creators. Our Text\\-to\\-Speech platforms help developers build natural, responsive voice agents and enable enterprise teams to produce high\\-quality voiceovers and multilingual dubs with ease.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Some interesting facts about Murf AI:** \n\n\n\n\n \u25cfCustomers in 100\\+ countries\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf 8Mn\\+ registered users\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf 200\\+ voices in 35\\+ languages offered by Murf Studio\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Rated by G2 as Top 10 Fastest Growing Products in 2024 \\& 2025\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf We are working on bleeding\\-edge research problems, in synthetic speech, and dubbing\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Job Summary** \n\n\n\n\n We're looking for a Content Marketer to write, edit, and scale content across Murf's organic channels. You'll be part of the organic growth team to turn keywords/topics/customer queries into original blogs, landing pages, product teardowns, and product\\-led content \u2014 and you'll do it at a volume and quality bar that's only possible with AI\\-native workflows.\n \n\n\n\n This is not a \"write three blogs a month\" role. We want someone who treats content production as a system: building briefs, running AI\\-assisted drafting pipelines, editing for accuracy and voice, and using data to decide what gets written next. We are looking for someone who can write genuinely helpful content that\u2019s not a summary of a few articles from the internet.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Key Responsibilities** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Content Production \\& Scale** \n\n\n\n\n Write and edit content across Murf's organic channels \u2014 long\\-form blogs, landing pages, use\\-case and comparison pages, glossary and help content \u2014 aligned to search, customer queries and search\\-intent strategy.\n \n\n\n\n Own the throughput and quality of the content pipeline: briefs in, publish\\-ready pages out, with clear turnaround times and quality gates\n \n\n\n\n Operate and improve AI\\-native content workflows (LLM\\-assisted research, brief generation, drafting, humanizing, and pre\\-publish audits)\n \n\n\n\n Refresh and consolidate existing content based on decay, cannibalization, and ranking data\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**SEO Collaboration** \n\n\n\n\n Partner with the SEO team on keyword research, SERP analysis, and content gap identification\n \n\n\n\n Structure content for search \u2014 headings, entities, internal links, human\\-friendly formatting \u2014 and for AI search surfaces (AI Overviews, LLM citations)\n \n\n\n\n Track performance in Google Search Console, Ahrefs, and analytics dashboards; use the data to prioritize what to write, update, or retire\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Product \\& Brand Accuracy** \n\n\n\n\n Work closely with product, design, and customer\\-facing teams so content accurately reflects Murf's features, use cases, and positioning\n \n\n\n\n Maintain Murf's tone of voice and editorial standards across every piece, whether written by a human, an AI, or both\n \n\n\n\n Contribute to content guidelines, style rules, and QC checklists that keep quality consistent as volume grows\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Required Skills and Qualifications** \n\n\n\n* 3\\+ years of experience in content marketing, with a strong focus on SEO and organic growth\n* Must have: prior experience at a B2B SaaS company, writing for technical or semi\\-technical buyers\n* Well versed in AI\\-native content workflows \u2014 you've used LLMs (Claude, ChatGPT, or similar) in a real production setting, not just for one\\-off drafts, and you have a point of view on where AI helps and where it hurts\n* Genuine comfort with AI and technology as subject matter \u2014 you can explain how AI agents, voice AI and LLMs work to a non\\-expert reader without getting it wrong\n* Working knowledge of SEO tools (Google Search Console, Analytics, Ahrefs or SEMrush) and the ability to analyze data\n* Strong portfolio of published content with demonstrable ranking or traffic results\n* Excellent editorial judgment: you can tell a good draft from a mediocre one and know exactly what to fix\n* Structured, systems\\-minded approach to production \u2014 you think in briefs, templates, and repeatable processes\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Good to Have** \n\n\n\n* Computer science or engineering background, or equivalent technical fluency\n* Hands\\-on experience with content automation (e.g., multi\\-step LLM pipelines, MCP\\-connected tools, no\\-code/low\\-code automation)\n* Familiarity with CMS platforms (Webflow, WordPress, headless CMS) and basic HTML/Markdown\n* Experience writing for developer or API audience\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Why Murf.ai?** \n\n\n\n\n Murf AI is revolutionizing creative workflows for businesses through the utilization of our cutting\\-edge AI technology. Recognized as a consistent Leader and Momentum Leader on G2 in 2022 and 2023, we empower L\\&D and creative teams to evolve into dynamic creative powerhouses. With a focus on cutting\\-edge research and innovation, a positive work culture, and real impact in the AI\\-driven space, Murf.ai is one of the fastest\\-growing companies in the AI voice space. Join us at this pivotal moment, where your ideas matter, and your leadership can leave a lasting impact. If you're ready for a challenge and have the vision to lead from the front, Murf.ai is where your journey into the next chapter of AI innovation begins.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466265305","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466265305"},{"title":"Creative Strategist & Copywriter","company":"GOOD MONK (Superfoods Valley Pvt. Ltd.)","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468354842","source":"linkedin","experience":"5 Yrs","skills":[103,107,109],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**About Superfoods Valley:** \n\n\n\n\n Superfoods Valley is a fast\\-growing nutrition\\-focused startup on a mission to make everyday nutrition simple, accessible, and effective for Indian families. Through our science\\-backed products and purpose\\-driven storytelling, we aim to bridge the nutrition gap in daily diets\u2014without changing taste, smell, or food habits.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Website:\n **www.goodmonk.in** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Key Responsibilities:** \n\n\n\n\n 1\\. Develop \\& Execute Creative Strategy for Good Monk. Take ownership of brand\u2019s Creative Output across formats \u2013 including Performance Creatives \\& Brand Campaigns\n \n\n\n\n 2\\. Ensure coherence of Brand Voice across all creative touchpoints\n \n\n\n\n 3\\. Gather a solid understanding of Who the Category \\& Brand consumer is and Why they buy (Pain Points / Desires). Use this effectively to build Creative Strategy \\& drive its Execution\n \n\n\n\n 4\\. Create High Performing Direct Response Creatives for Performance Marketing. Own the entire process \\& final output. Concept, Script, oversee the Shoot wherever required (internal / external), Final Output. This will include various kinds of creatives \u2013 Videos \\& Statics \u2013 UGC, Influencers, Product Centric etc\n \n\n\n\n 5\\. Be on top of creative performance: What\u2019s Working \\& What Not; and Why\n \n\n\n\n 6\\.Collaborate effectively with Internal teams (Performance, Writers, Designers / Editors, R\\&D, Nutrition) \\& External Agencies to create compelling creatives, in line with business goals\n \n\n\n\n 7\\. Conduct research and gather insights to inform copywriting strategy\n \n\n\n\n 8\\.Strengthen the ecosystem of best in class, fit for purpose Creative partners to work with\n \n\n\n\n 9\\. Stay up\\-to\\-date with industry trends \\& best practices in Direct Response Copywriting \\& Brand Storytelling\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**What We\u2019re Looking For:** \n\n\n\n\n \u20222\\-5 years of relevant experience in creative strategy, advertising, content, or brand building.\n \n\n\n\n \u2022Proven track record of working on consumer brands\u2014preferably D2C, FMCG, Health \\& Wellness\n \n\n\n\n \u2022Strong grasp of digital\\-first storytelling and brand thinking.\n \n\n\n\n \u2022A sharp eye for copy, design, and visual storytelling.\n \n\n\n\n \u2022Excellent communication and presentation skills.\n \n\n\n\n \u2022Comfortable managing creative workflows with external partners and in\\-house teams.\n \n\n\n\n \u2022Passionate about purpose\\-driven brands and the health \\& wellness space.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Why Join Us?** \n\n\n\n\n \u2022Be part of a purpose\\-led, growing brand shaping the future of family nutrition.\n \n\n\n\n \u2022Work closely with a passionate founding team and category experts.\n \n\n\n\n \u2022A culture that encourages ideas, ownership, and experimentation.\n \n\n\n\n \u2022Opportunity to create content that educates, empowers, and impacts lives.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**What We Offer:** \n\n\n\n\n \u2022Competitive salary and benefits package.\n \n\n\n\n \u2022Opportunity to work in a dynamic and creative environment.\n \n\n\n\n \u2022Professional development and growth opportunities.\n \n\n\n\n \u2022WFO role. Office in Ulsoor, Bengaluru","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468354842","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468354842"},{"title":"Associate Director - Category","company":"Pocket FM","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467173648","source":"linkedin","experience":"Manager","skills":[104],"is_walkin":false,"description":"At Pocket, we\u2019ve experienced rapid growth in both revenue and scale over the past few years, further fueling our ambition. With a long\\-term vision, we are well\\-positioned and well\\-capitalized to drive sustained expansion.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n We operate across diverse industries and geographies, tackling complex challenges that require leaders who can navigate ambiguity and drive impact. These roles demand the ability to solve novel, first\\-of\\-their\\-kind problems\u2014often without precedent. Thriving at Pocket requires a mix of high IQ and EQ, analytical rigor, and an entrepreneurial mindset.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n We offer ambitious goals, complex problem\\-solving, and full ownership over execution. Prior experience solving similar problems isn\u2019t required. What matters is adaptability, a willingness to learn and reinvent, and intellectual humility.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**You\u2019ll be solving for one of these problem statements:** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* **Customer Lifecycle Growth \\& Retention** \n : Drive engagement, retention, and monetization across the user lifecycle with a deep focus on building scalable retention loops and improving lifetime value\n* **Content\\-Led Growth \\& Expansion** \n : Drive the content charter for retention, scaling high\\-performing content to reach new audience segments while supporting launches in new markets\n* **Data\\-Driven Experimentation** \n : Move beyond traditional acquisition experiments to test, iterate, and scale initiatives that deepen user engagement, taking inspiration from gaming industry retention models\n* **Cross\\-Functional Leadership** \n : Partner with content, product, and analytics teams to design and execute experiments that drive sustainable growth, leveraging insights to inform scalable strategies across diverse genres\n* **Scaling** \n : Leverage AI\\-native workflows to automate and personalize lifecycle interventions, enhancing retention and monetization at scale\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Here\u2019s what we are looking for:** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* Astute problem\\-solving skills and the ability to break (seemingly) large problems into smaller, practical, solvable pieces with a data\\-driven approach to decision\\-making\n* Someone who excels at developing and implementing a plan from concept to completion, generating measurable outcomes across retention, engagement, and monetization\n* Track record of productive teamwork\u2014starts with \u201cwhy\u201d rather than \u201cwhat,\u201d enjoys getting hands dirty, and possesses a drive for continuous learning\n* A deep understanding of user needs, preferably gained in consumer\\-first companies\n* Comfort working with AI automation tools and exposure to LLM\\-based workflows to drive scalable growth initiatives\n* Action bias: solves problems, executes, and iterates as needed","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467173648","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467173648"},{"title":"Content Creator","company":"RK Group","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466869013","source":"linkedin","is_walkin":false,"description":"**Content Creator \\& Planner**\n\n\n\n\n 1\\. Plan and maintain monthly content calendars across all social media platforms. Brainstorm and develop content ideas aligned with brand goals, campaigns, festivals, and audience interests.\n \n\n\n\n 2\\. Coordinate with cross departments to understand content requirements and obtain approvals.\n \n\n\n\n 3\\. Plan end\\-to\\-end content shoots, including locations, props, references, and shot lists.\n \n\n\n\n 4\\. Lead shoots to ensure the planned content is captured correctly.\n \n\n\n\n 5\\. Review raw photos and videos after the shoot to ensure they match the brief.\n \n\n\n\n 6\\. Organize and hand over labelled files with clear editing instructions to the editor and use AI to create creatives.\n \n\n\n\n 7\\. Track content timelines and ensure all deliverables are completed on schedule.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466869013","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466869013"},{"title":"Video Editing and AI Content Intern (Short-Form)","company":"AbhyasX","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467109939","source":"linkedin","experience":"Intern","skills":[107,117],"is_walkin":false,"description":"Company Description\n \n\n\n\n AbhyasX is India's AI\\-powered exam preparation platform for UPSC and state civil services aspirants. The platform offers AI\\-curated daily current affairs, a 17,000\\+ question PYQ bank spanning 31 years, AI\\-driven Mains answer evaluation, and structured mind maps, along with bilingual (Kannada\\-English) content for KPSC aspirants. Trusted by 1,000\\+ learners across Karnataka, AbhyasX combines deep civil services expertise with cutting\\-edge AI to help aspirants study smarter.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Role Description\n \n\n\n\n This is an on\\-site Video Editing and AI Content Intern role based in Bengaluru. You will create short\\-form videos for two streams: marketing content for AbhyasX, and short\\-form content for our AI courses. You will get hands\\-on experience with AI video tools like Higgsfield alongside traditional editing software, and work directly with the founder on content that reaches thousands of aspirants.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Duration: 3 months\n \n\n\n\n Possibility of a full\\-time offer based on performance\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n What You Will Do\n \n\n\n\n \\- Create short\\-form marketing videos for AbhyasX: product demos, feature highlights, exam tips, and current affairs hooks\n \n\n\n\n \\- Produce short\\-form content for AI courses: concept explainers, tool walkthroughs, and bite\\-sized lessons\n \n\n\n\n \\- Use AI video tools (Higgsfield, Runway, Kling, HeyGen, or similar) to generate visuals, B\\-roll, avatars, and effects\n \n\n\n\n \\- Edit footage into 15 to 90 second videos with strong hooks, captions, music, and transitions\n \n\n\n\n \\- Adapt content for Instagram Reels, YouTube Shorts, and LinkedIn\n \n\n\n\n \\- Keep up with content trends and new AI tools, and experiment with new formats\n \n\n\n\n \\- Help maintain a consistent AbhyasX visual style\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n What We Are Looking For\n \n\n\n\n \\- Students or recent graduates with a passion for video and social media content\n \n\n\n\n \\- Basic to intermediate skills in any editing tool (Premiere Pro, DaVinci Resolve, CapCut, or similar)\n \n\n\n\n \\- Curiosity about AI tools; prior use of Higgsfield, Runway, or similar is a big plus\n \n\n\n\n \\- A good sense of what makes short\\-form content engaging\n \n\n\n\n \\- Willingness to learn fast, take feedback, and work on multiple videos a week\n \n\n\n\n \\- Kannada or Hindi proficiency is a plus\n \n\n\n\n \\- Interest in edtech, AI, or civil services is an advantage\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n What You Will Gain\n \n\n\n\n \\- Real\\-world experience building content for an AI startup\n \n\n\n\n \\- Hands\\-on work with the latest AI video and content tools\n \n\n\n\n \\- Direct mentorship from the founder\n \n\n\n\n \\- Published work for your portfolio\n \n\n\n\n \\- Certificate of internship and letter of recommendation for strong performers\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n To apply, share a few samples of videos you have edited or created (personal projects, college work, or social media content all count).","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467109939","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467109939"},{"title":"Visual & Creative Design Intern","company":"Leadzo","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467159986","source":"linkedin","experience":"Intern","skills":[45,103,105,107,115,116,117],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**Social Media, Website, Product \\& Brand Design** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**\u201cWe\u2019re looking for someone who doesn\u2019t just make things look good, but someone who can take an idea, turn it into a strong visual, and own the design from concept to final execution.\u201d** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**About the company** \n\n\n\n\n**Leadzo (** \n www.leadzo.co.in) is building a modern lead generation and service marketplace platform designed to connect customers with verified service professionals across service industries, from Marketing \\& Technology, Legal \\& Business, Home Services, Health \\& Wellbeing, Construction \\& Trades, Lessons \\& Training, Events \\& Creative, and more.\n \n\n\n\n Our mission: to make it easier, faster, and more transparent for people to discover and hire trusted professionals online, while helping businesses grow through qualified, high\\-intent leads.\n \n\n\n\n Our platform is live pan\\-India, with active buyers and sellers across the country. We are now in a crucial scale and stabilization phase, improving the product, strengthening our brand, and building a stronger digital presence across our website, product, marketing channels, and social media.\n \n\n\n\n Design plays a major role in that. From a social media post and website banner to a product screen or campaign creative, we want every visual interaction with Leadzo to feel clear, modern, consistent, and purposeful.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**About the role** \n\n\n\n\n**We are looking for a** \n**Visual \\& Creative Design Intern** \n who wants to work across different areas of digital design rather than being restricted to one type of creative work.\n \n\n\n\n You will work on\n **social media creatives, website banners, marketing campaigns, presentations, product visuals, website screens, mobile app screens, and other digital assets** \n .\n \n\n\n\n This is a hands\\-on role. You won\u2019t just receive a brief, create one design, and move on. You\u2019ll be expected to understand the objective, explore different creative directions, execute the design, take feedback, and improve it.\n \n\n\n\n You will work closely with the\n **Marketing, Product, and Development teams** \n , giving you exposure to how design is actually used inside a growing technology company.\n \n\n\n\n We\u2019re looking for someone with strong creative instincts, attention to detail, curiosity, and the willingness to learn quickly.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Key Responsibilities** \n\n\n\n* Create\n **social media posts, carousels, infographics, promotional creatives, and campaign visuals** \n for platforms such as Instagram and LinkedIn.\n* Design\n **website banners, landing page creatives, promotional sections, pop\\-ups, and other website assets** \n .\n* Create visual creatives for performance marketing and promotional campaigns.\n* Work on\n **website and mobile app screens** \n when required.\n* Create wireframes, mockups, prototypes, and polished digital designs.\n* Develop creative concepts and visual directions for campaigns and new initiatives.\n* Maintain consistency in Leadzo\u2019s visual identity across different platforms.\n* Adapt designs into different sizes and formats for various digital channels.\n* Create presentations and other marketing/design collateral when required.\n* Work with the marketing team to turn campaign ideas into compelling visual communication.\n* Work with the product and development teams to create clean, practical digital interfaces.\n* Take feedback positively and iterate quickly.\n* Maintain organised Figma files, components, templates, and design assets.\n* Research current design trends and bring fresh creative ideas to the team.\n* Continuously improve the quality and consistency of Leadzo's visual communication.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Tools \\& Skills** \n\n\n\n\n**Must have:** \n\n\n\n* Good working knowledge of\n **Figma**\n* **Strong understanding of basic design principles**\n* **Good eye for typography, spacing, composition, colours, and visual hierarchy**\n* **Ability to create clean and modern digital creatives**\n* **Basic understanding of responsive design**\n* **Ability to work across multiple creative formats**\n* **Strong attention to detail**\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Good to have:** \n\n\n\n* Adobe Photoshop\n* Adobe Illustrator\n* Canva\n* Basic motion graphics/video editing\n* After Effects\n* Premiere Pro\n* Basic understanding of UI/UX\n* Experience designing websites or mobile apps\n* Experience creating social media creatives\n\n\n\n You do not need to know every tool listed above.\n **Strong design fundamentals and a good portfolio matter more than the number of tools you know.** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**What We\u2019re Looking For** \n\n\n\n\n**We\u2019re looking for someone who:** \n\n\n\n* Thinks creatively instead of simply following templates.\n* Can take a rough idea and turn it into a polished visual.\n* Has a strong eye for detail.\n* Understands that good design is both\n **visually appealing and purposeful** \n .\n* Is comfortable receiving feedback and improving their work.\n* Can manage multiple design requirements.\n* Is curious about how websites, apps, products, and marketing work.\n* Takes ownership of their work instead of waiting for step\\-by\\-step instructions.\n* Wants to build a strong portfolio through real\\-world projects.\n\n\n\n**Portfolio Is Important** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Your portfolio matters more than your degree.** \n\n\n\n\n**You can share:** \n\n\n\n* College projects\n* Personal design projects\n* Social media creatives\n* Website designs\n* App designs\n* Branding projects\n* Posters\n* Illustrations\n* Freelance work\n* Concept designs\n* Any other digital design work\n\n\n\n Even if you don't have professional experience, we want to see\n **how you think and what you can create** \n .\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**What Will Get You Rejected** \n\n\n\n* You only know how to edit existing Canva templates.\n* You cannot explain the thinking behind your designs.\n* You copy designs without understanding the visual structure.\n* You are unwilling to take feedback or make iterations.\n* You have no interest in learning beyond social media posts.\n* You need detailed instructions for every small design task.\n* You prioritise making something flashy over making it clear and useful.\n* You have no portfolio or design samples to show.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**What You Get** \n\n\n\n* **\u20b920,000/month internship stipend**\n* **Hands\\-on experience working on a live technology platform.**\n* **Exposure to** \n**social media, marketing, website, product, mobile app, and brand design** \n .\n* Opportunity to work directly with marketing, product, and development teams.\n* Real\\-world projects that can become part of your professional portfolio.\n* Opportunity to learn how design connects with marketing, product, and business objectives.\n* A fast\\-paced environment where you can experiment, learn, and take ownership.\n* Potential opportunity to continue with the company based on performance and business requirements.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Office Location:** \n Bengaluru / Bangalore, India\n \n\n\n\n**Internship Type:** \n Full\\-time, Work From Office\n \n\n\n\n**Stipend:** \n \u20b920,000 per month","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467159986","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467159986"},{"title":"Sr Manager | Director - Media Planning","company":"WPP Media","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468360874","source":"linkedin","experience":"6+ Yrs","skills":[103,104,107],"is_walkin":false,"description":"****About WPP Media****\n WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world\u2019s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world\\-class partnerships \u2013 all united by our\u202fpioneering\u202fagentic marketing platform, WPP Open \u2013 we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth.\n   \n\n  \n\n WPP Media is WPP's AI\\-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.\n   \n\n  \n\n For more information, visit wppmedia.com.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Sr Manager \\| Director \\- Implementation Planning, GOC**\n****About WPP Media****\n WPP is the creative transformation company. We use the power of creativity to build better futures for our people, planet, clients and communities. For more information, visit wpp.com.\n   \n\n  \n\n WPP Media is WPP\u2019s global media collective. In a world where media is everywhere and in everything, we bring the best platform, people, and partners together to create limitless opportunities for growth. For more information, visit wppmedia.com\n   \n\n  \n\n At WPP Media, We Believe In The Power Of Our Culture And Our People. It\u2019s What Elevates Us To Deliver Exceptional Experiences For Both Our Clients And Each Other. In This Role It Will Be Critical To Embrace WPP \\& WPP Media\u2019s Shared Core Values:\n   \n\n  \n\n* Be Extraordinary by Leading Collectively to Inspire transformational Creativity.\n* Create an Open environment by Balancing People and Client Experiences by Cultivating Trust.\n* Lead Optimistically by Championing Growth and Development to Mobilize the Enterprise.\n\n\n****Role Summary And Impact****\n As part of our Global Operations Centre (GOC), you will partner with teams across the U.S., Europe, and Asia to deliver high\\-impact, integrated media planning solutions across multiple markets and channels.\n   \n\n  \n\n* Lead end\\-to\\-end planning operations across multiple campaigns, brands, or markets while ensuring consistency in quality, timelines, and strategic output.\n* Support Associate Directors and market stakeholders in developing integrated media planning recommendations aligned with business and campaign objectives.\n* Act as a key escalation point for operational and planning\\-related challenges across the team.\n* Drive excellence in campaign planning deliverables, including audience strategy, channel allocation, forecasting, reporting frameworks, and post\\-campaign analysis.\n* Collaborate closely with Activation, Ad Operations, Analytics, and Client Servicing teams to ensure seamless execution of media plans.\n* Ensure planning best practices, governance standards, and documentation processes are consistently followed across the team.\n* Support implementation and adoption of planning tools, automation solutions, and operational efficiencies.\n* Monitor team productivity, delivery quality, and workload allocation to ensure optimal operational performance.\n* Provide coaching, mentorship, and developmental guidance to Managers, Senior Executives, and Executives.\n* Contribute to capability\\-building initiatives, knowledge\\-sharing forums, and process improvement projects.\n* Foster a collaborative and high\\-performing team culture focused on accountability, innovation, and continuous learning.\n\n\n****Skills And Experience****\n* Media Planning teams are experts on the digital media landscape and how consumers interact with it. We architect and steward holistic media plans throughout their lifecycle, owning the creation of overall plans, cross\\-channel budget allocation, in\\-flight cross\\-channel optimization \\& reporting and post\\-campaign analysis. We are our clients\u2019 key contacts for a unified view across all aspects of their campaigns, narrating the story of the campaign from planning recommendation through to PCA.\n* 6 plus years of experience in media planning, integrated communications planning, or digital strategy roles, preferably within a global agency environment.\n* Strong understanding of integrated media channels including digital, social, search, commerce, video, programmatic, impact buys and other non biddable emerging media.\n* Proven experience managing teams in a fast\\-paced offshore/onshore delivery setup.\n* Experience handling multi\\-market campaigns and collaborating with global stakeholders.\n* Strong operational mindset with experience managing workflows, quality standards, and process governance.\n* Excellent analytical and strategic thinking capabilities with a data\\-driven approach to planning and optimization.\n* Strong communication and stakeholder management skills with the ability to influence and collaborate effectively.\n* Experience with media planning tools, reporting dashboards, and planning frameworks.\n* Strong presentation and storytelling capabilities.\n* Ability to identify process improvement opportunities and drive operational efficiencies.\n* Strong coaching and people management skills with experience developing high\\-performing teams.\n* Ability to manage multiple priorities and operate effectively in a dynamic environment.\n\n\n****Life At WPP Media \\& Benefits****\n Our passion for shaping the next era of media includes investing in our employees to help them do their best work, and we\u2019re just as committed to employee growth as we are to responsible media investment. WPP Media employees can tap into the global WPP Media \\& WPP networks to pursue their passions, grow their networks, and learn at the cutting edge of marketing and advertising. We have a variety of employee resource groups and host frequent in\\-office events showcasing team wins, sharing thought leadership, and celebrating holidays and milestone events. Our benefits include access to internal learning platforms, certifications, and training sessions, life insurance, wellness programs, significant paid time off, preferential partner discounts, employee mental health awareness day, and more.\n   \n\n  \n\n Research shows that candidates from underrepresented backgrounds often don't apply for roles if they don't meet all the criteria.\u202fAt WPP Media, we strongly encourage you to apply if you\u2019re interested, we'd love to know how you can positively impact our team with your experience!\n   \n\n  \n\n As an Equal Opportunities Employer, we believe that diversity is vital and positively influences the environment in which we operate. We are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive work environment that is free of discrimination, harassment or bullying. Race, colour, ancestry, religion, gender, gender identity, national origin, sexual orientation, age, marital status or disability status have no bearing on our hiring decisions, and we encourage all applicants.\n   \n\n  \n\n We view everyone as an individual and we understand that inclusion is more than just diversity \u2013 it\u2019s about belonging. We celebrate the fact that everyone is unique and that\u2019s what makes us so good at what we do. We pride ourselves on being a company that embraces difference and truly represents the global clients we work with.\n   \n\n  \n\n We believe the best work happens when we're together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That's why we\u2019ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.\n   \n\n  \n\n Please read our Privacy Notice (\n **https://www.wppmedia.com/pages/privacy\\-policy** \n ) for more information on how we process the information you provide.\n   \n\n  \n\n While we appreciate all applications received, only those candidates selected for an interview will be contacted.\n   \n\n  \n\n Please read our Privacy Notice for more information on how we process the information you provide.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468360874","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468360874"},{"title":"Content Writer - Team Lead [ Apply only if you're in Bengaluru ] | 3\u20135 Years | Onsite-Bengaluru | Up to \u20b97.5 LPA | Immediate Joiners Only","company":"Hello Mentor","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467181530","source":"linkedin","experience":"5 Yrs","skills":[100,103,104,105,107,108,109],"is_walkin":false,"description":"Job Title: Content Writer \\- Team Lead\n \n\n\n\n Experience: 3\u20135 Years\n \n\n\n\n Location: JP Nagar, Bengaluru\n \n\n\n\n Work Mode: Full\\-Time \\| On\\-Site \\| 6Days\n \n\n\n\n CTC: Up to \u20b9 7\\.5 LPA\n \n\n\n\n Notice Period: Immediate to 7 Days\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Role Overview :** \n\n\n\n\n We are looking for a strategic, research\\-oriented Head of Content \\& Growth to lead our content marketing function and drive organic growth through impactful content and SEO initiatives with strong expertise in writing high\\-quality, research\\-backed blogs and articles. The role will focus on SEO, market and competitor research, content strategy, and creating informative content that drives organic traffic, engagement, and lead generation.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Key Responsibilities :** \n\n\n\n* Develop and execute content marketing \\& SEO strategies.\n* Plan and manage the content calendar.\n* Create and Optimize blogs, landing pages, product pages, case studies, and marketing content.\n* Experience in researching, writing, and publishing high\\-quality blogs and articles.\n* Conduct keyword research, content audits, and competitor analysis.\n* Improve organic traffic, keyword rankings, and lead generation.\n* Collaborate with Product, Design, Development, and Marketing teams.\n* Lead, mentor, and review the Content team.\n* Track content performance using analytics and optimize campaigns.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Required Skills:** \n\n\n\n* Content Marketing \\& Growth Strategy\n* SEO Strategy \\& Keyword Research\n* Content Planning \\& Editorial Management\n* Copywriting, Editing \\& Content Optimization\n* Product \\& Technical Content Writing\n* Brand Storytelling \\& Thought Leadership\n* Marketing Analytics \\& Performance Tracking\n* Team Leadership, Mentoring \\& Development\n* Project Management \\& Cross\\-Functional Stakeholder Management\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Qualifications :** \n\n\n\n* Master\u2019s Degree in Marketing, Communications, Business Administration, Journalism, Mass Communication, or a related field \u2013 Mandatory\n* 3\u20135 years of relevant experience in Content Marketing, Content Strategy, SEO, or Digital Marketing\n* Proven experience in leading and mentoring content teams\n* Strong analytical, communication, writing, and stakeholder\\-management skills\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Tools :** \n\n\n\n* Google Analytics\n* Google Search Console\n* Google Tag Manager\n* SEMrush\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Perks and Benefits :** \n\n\n\n* Paid Annual Leaves\n* PF \\& Health Insurance\n* Team Lunches\n* Long New Year Vacation\n* Learning \\& Career Growth","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467181530","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467181530"},{"title":"Social Media Strategist","company":"Prashanthi Balamandira Trust","location":"Remote","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468608201","source":"linkedin","experience":"5 Yrs","skills":[100,103,104,107],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**About the Company** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Sri Madhusudan Sai Global Humanitarian Mission passionately provides free Nutrition, Education, and Healthcare to those in need across 100 countries. Under the visionary leadership of the globally acclaimed humanitarian, Sri Madhusudan Sai, the organisation is dedicated to uplifting the most marginalised communities. The mission is grounded in the ethos of selfless service, guided by the belief that all are a part of \u2018One World, One Family\u2019.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**About the Role** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n The Social Media Strategist role will involve crafting impactful campaigns that resonate with our values and vision. By staying abreast of the latest social media trends and technologies, you'll ensure our message reaches the right audience. Collaborating closely with our project and communications teams, you'll help manage our online reputation and leverage data\\-driven insights to optimise our social media presence.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Responsibilities** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* Transform our social media presence with groundbreaking strategies that resonate with our audience and powerfully convey our message.\n* Collaborate closely with the project and communications teams to create cohesive and impactful social awareness strategies and campaigns.\n* Demonstrate expertise in navigating and utilising major social media platforms, including Facebook, Twitter, YouTube, Instagram, and other popular apps.\n* Stay up\\-to\\-date with the latest social media trends, technologies, and best practices to ensure the organisation maintains a strong online presence.\n* Handle online reputation management and social listening activities to monitor the organisation's brand image and respond to discussions and inquiries.\n* Leverage data analytics and insights to measure the performance of social media campaigns, identify opportunities for improvement, and make data\\-driven decisions.\n* Organise and host external events, such as community events and competitions, to further engage the organisation's online following.\n* Continuously explore new and innovative ways to leverage social media to support the organisation's mission and objectives.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Qualifications** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Communications, Digital Media, or a related field.\n* Minimum 5 years of experience in social media strategy, management, and content creation.\n* Proven track record of developing and executing successful social media campaigns.\n* Familiarity with social media management tools and analytics platforms.\n* Experience in event planning and community engagement is an added advantage.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Required Skills** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* Exceptional strategic and creative thinking skills to conceptualise and execute engaging social media campaigns.\n* Proficiency in managing and leveraging major social media platforms, including Facebook, Twitter, YouTube, and Instagram.\n* Strong understanding of social media trends, emerging technologies, and best practices.\n* Ability to collaborate effectively with cross\\-functional teams.\n* Data\\-driven approach to social media analytics and performance optimisation.\n* Excellent written and verbal communication skills to articulate ideas and strategies.\n* Proactive and adaptable mindset to respond to changing social media landscape.\n* Project management skills and ability to work under tight deadlines.\n* Creativity and passion for leveraging social media to drive organisational goals.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Preferred Skills** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* Experience in event planning and community engagement is an added advantage.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Pay range and compensation package** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n This is a fully remote position, offering the flexibility to work from home on a full\\-time basis.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Equal Opportunity Statement** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Joining SMSGHM offers a chance to impact marginalised communities globally. With a focus on free Nutrition, Education, and Healthcare across 32 countries, your efforts directly contribute to positive change. Being part of our mission means experiencing the joy of helping others and knowing your contributions bring happiness to those in need.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468608201","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468608201"},{"title":"Business Development Executive","company":"Asha Sweet Center","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4465264354","source":"linkedin","experience":"2 Yrs","skills":[103,105,106,107,108],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**Brand:** \n Asha Sweet Center\n \n\n\n\n**Location:** \n Bangalore\n \n\n\n\n**Experience:** \n 1\u20132 years / Freshers welcome\n \n\n\n\n**Type:** \n Full Time\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n BUSINESS DEVELOPMENT EXECUTIVE\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Key Responsibilities\n \n\n\n* **Social Media Planning:** \n Work closely with the social media team on social media calendar planning and ensure timely execution of planned content.\n* **Photo Shoot Planning \\& Coordination:** \n Schedule and coordinate product photo shoots with the relevant teams, ensuring that all products, equipment, props, and other requirements are arranged and ready before the shoot.\n* **E\\-commerce \\& Platform Coordination:** \n Coordinate with Swiggy, Zomato, Amazon, other quick\\-commerce platforms, the company website, and retail managers to understand and fulfil product shoot requirements as per their respective specifications and guidelines.\n* **Product Coordination with Factory \\& Stores:** \n Coordinate and follow up with the factory for the supply of products required for shoots. Ensure that all products are accounted for and returned to the designated person at the factory/store after the shoot.\n* **External Vendor Management:** \n Coordinate with external vendors, including marketing agencies, printing companies, advertisers, and other service providers, as and when required.\n* **Business Development \\& Lead Generation:** \n Identify potential business opportunities, events, corporate offices, exhibitions, and other avenues where the brand can establish a presence through stalls, stores, kiosks, corporate partnerships, or other relevant formats.\n* **Digital Marketing Oversight:** \n Review and develop a strong technical and analytical understanding of SEO, SEM, Google Ads, Meta Ads, and other digital marketing plans proposed by the Grocat team. Present recommendations and observations to management and ensure that agreed action points are followed up and implemented. Also ensure that Google Reviews are monitored and responded to appropriately and promptly.\n* **Content \\& Social Media Oversight:** \n Monitor scheduled posts and content published across various digital channels, ensuring that the content is accurate, timely, and aligned with the brand. Ensure sufficient content is planned and available well in advance.\n* **Offline Marketing:** \n Explore, plan, and coordinate offline marketing initiatives and other relevant marketing channels to strengthen brand visibility and reach.\n* **Technology \\& Tool Research:** \n Research and evaluate relevant tools, software, platforms, and technologies that can improve business operations, marketing effectiveness, or overall efficiency. Bring relevant recommendations to the attention of senior management and follow up on implementation after approval.\n* **Design Coordination:** \n Coordinate with in\\-house and external designers for the development of menus, signboards, packaging/boxes, pamphlets, catalogues, promotional material, and other brand collaterals.\n* **Shoot Equipment Management:** \n Safely maintain and manage all photo/video shoot equipment, props, and other related assets under their custody and ensure they are stored and handled responsibly.\n* **Management Reporting:** \n Present ongoing progress, upcoming plans, key initiatives, and projects in the pipeline to senior management on a fortnightly or monthly basis, as required.\n\n\n\n DESIRED QUALITIES \\& SKILLS\n \n\n\n* Technically proficient in\n **SEO, SEM, Google Ads, Meta Ads** \n , and other digital marketing tools is a plus.\n* Comfortable and proficient in using\n **Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn, YouTube** \n , and other relevant social media platforms.\n* Proficient in the use of\n **AI tools** \n for research, content creation, analysis, planning, and improving work efficiency.\n* **Excellent follow\\-up skills** \n with a strong sense of urgency and prompt execution.\n* A\n **good collaborator** \n who can effectively work with internal teams and external partners.\n* **Extroverted and confident** \n , with strong networking and relationship\\-building skills.\n* **Dedicated, diligent, patient, and responsible** \n , with the ability to manage multiple tasks simultaneously.\n* **Creative and resourceful** \n , while being mindful of budget constraints, especially during the initial stages.\n* An\n **effective planner** \n who can create practical, realistic, and executable plans and ensure they are followed through to completion.\n* Strong\n **communication, coordination, and problem\\-solving skills** \n .\n* Ability to take\n **ownership of tasks** \n and see them through from planning to execution.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4465264354","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4465264354"},{"title":"Account Strategist, Commerce, Mid-Market Sales, Google Customer Solutions","company":"Google","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4448549255","source":"linkedin","experience":"2 Yrs","skills":[105,106,107,113],"is_walkin":false,"description":"Note: By applying to this position you will have an opportunity to share your preferred working location from the following:\n **Gurugram, Haryana, India; Bengaluru, Karnataka, India; Mumbai, Maharashtra, India** \n .\n **Minimum qualifications:**\n* Bachelor's degree or equivalent practical experience.\n* 2 years of experience in sales, business development, advertising, account management, marketing, or consulting.\n\n\n**Preferred qualifications:**\n* 2 years of Industry experience in digital advertising, consultative sales, business development, or digital marketing, working with advertisers, agencies, or clients in India.\n* Ability to strategically assess and solve customer needs via sales techniques, including effective questioning, objection management, investigative skills, and engaging selling.\n* Ability to build compelling narratives and utilize storytelling as an engagement strategy.\n* Ability to think strategically about complex issues to develop recommendations/action plans.\n* Ability to travel for customer meetings as needed, up to 10% to 20% of the time.\n\n\n**About the job** \n Businesses of all shapes and sizes rely on Google\u2019s unparalleled advertising solutions to help them grow in today's dynamic marketing environment. You bring a passion for sales, knowledge of online media, and commitment to maximize customer success. You act like an owner, move with velocity through change, finding innovative and strategic ways to consistently deliver extraordinary and incremental outcomes for both Google and your customers. You build trusted relationships with customers, uncovering their business needs and translating them into powerful solutions to achieve their most ambitious goals. You achieve as a team with sellers, shape the future of advertising in the AI\\-era, and make a real impact on the millions of companies and billions of users that trust Google with their most important goals. Google Customer Solutions (GCS) sales teams are trusted advisors and competitive sellers who maintain a relentless focus on customer success by bringing the best Google has to offer to small\\- and medium\\-sized businesses (SMBs), which are the backbone of our communities. As a member of our team, you\u2019ll have the opportunity to work with company owners and make a real difference in their businesses by helping them grow. Together, we help shape the future of innovation for customers, partners, and sellers...and we have fun doing it.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Responsibilities**\n* Manage a portfolio of businesses and develop a comprehensive understanding of their business challenges, marketing objectives, and success metrics.\n* Build an in\\-depth knowledge of how Google advertising products work and can be used to help meet a wide range of marketing objectives.\n* Build relationships with the end customer or agencies, and serve as a trusted advisor identifying opportunities for growth, creating multi\\-quarter plans, and driving adoption of key product best practices to grow their business with Google.\n* Collaborate within the team, and cross\\-functionally to execute plans and ensure accountability to meet or exceed goals.\n* Develop and refine a point of view to scale product, processes, and align priorities to drive customer growth, and help scale best practices to contribute to overall team success.\n\n\n Google is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements. See also Google's EEO Policy and EEO is the Law. If you have a disability or special need that requires accommodation, please let us know by completing our Accommodations for Applicants form .","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4448549255","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4448549255"},{"title":"Business Development Associate (Intern)","company":"Mindenious","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4465994961","source":"linkedin","experience":"Intern","skills":[103,105,106,107],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**Company Description** \n Mindenious is an innovative educational technology platform focused on bridging the gap between classroom learning and real\\-world industry requirements. The platform supports students through internships, personalized career guidance, and mentorship, helping them navigate dynamic professional landscapes. Mindenious emphasizes practical skill development and career readiness, encouraging learners to thrive rather than simply accumulate knowledge. The organization is committed to elevating intellect and empowering students to pursue meaningful, future\\-oriented careers.\n   \n\n**Role Description** \n The Business Development Associate (Intern) is a full\\-time, on\\-site role based in Bengaluru. The individual in this position will support business growth by identifying prospective partners, generating leads, and assisting in outreach activities to educational institutions and corporate organizations. Day\\-to\\-day responsibilities include conducting market research, preparing and delivering presentations about Mindenious\u2019s offerings, and maintaining accurate records of leads and interactions in internal systems. The role also involves coordinating with internal teams to refine value propositions, gathering feedback from prospects, and contributing to campaigns that promote internships, mentorship programs, and other services. The intern will work closely with senior team members to learn best practices in business development while actively participating in meetings and client communications.\n   \n\n**Qualifications**\n* Strong communication abilities, including clear verbal and written communication and professional interaction with diverse stakeholders.\n* Effective presentation skills, with experience in creating and delivering engaging presentations.\n* Lead generation skills, including identifying prospects, qualifying leads, and following up systematically.\n* Market research capabilities, such as analyzing trends, mapping competitors, and understanding student and institutional needs.\n* Basic understanding of sales or business development processes, preferably in ed\\-tech or related domains.\n* Ability to work on\\-site in Bengaluru on a full\\-time basis, manage time efficiently, and prioritize multiple tasks.\n* Comfort with using productivity tools (e.g., spreadsheets, presentation software, CRM or lead\\-tracking tools).\n* Current student or recent graduate in Business, Marketing, Management, or a related field is preferred; candidates from other disciplines with strong interest in business development are also encouraged to apply.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4465994961","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4465994961"},{"title":"Business Development Associate - Immediate Joiners","company":"Chain Reaction Co.","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468359810","source":"linkedin","ski