 Basic understanding of SEO\n   \n\n  \n\n Experience with WooCommerce, Shiprocket integrations, and dynamic content implementation\n   \n\n  \n\n Ability to improve the website\u2019s Core Web Vitals, overall Health Score, and performance\n   \n\n  \n\n Familiarity with WP Rocket or similar optimisation tools\n   \n\n  \n\n  \n\n Benefits\n   \n\n  \n\n Insurance and other benefits","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467192972","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467192972"},{"title":"Graphic Designer (Video + Statics)","company":"STRATIST","location":"Bangalore","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467508652","source":"linkedin","skills":[103,107,112,115,117],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**Company Description** \n Stratist is a full\\-stack healthcare growth and capability partner that helps hospitals, clinics, healthtech startups, and healthcare professionals scale clinically, operationally, digitally, and strategically. Through seven specialized verticals\u2014including marketing and growth, tech enablement, HR and talent, hospital operations, strategic advisory, branding and content, and training\u2014Stratist supports organizations across the healthcare ecosystem. The team focuses on sustainable business models, affordable digital transformation, and building high\\-performing, future\\-ready healthcare teams. Stratist emphasizes real\\-world outcomes such as more patients, better systems, and lower cost per lead, while championing the importance of storytelling, systems, and scale alongside clinical excellence. The company is actively involved in sharing healthcare growth insights, strategy tips, and professional development opportunities.\n \n\n\n\n**Role Description** \n The Graphic Designer (Video \\+ Statics) will create visual content for digital and offline channels, including static graphics, motion graphics, and video assets that support Stratist\u2019s healthcare growth initiatives. In this full\\-time on\\-site role based in Bangalore Urban, the designer will collaborate with marketing, branding, and content teams to translate campaign objectives into compelling visual stories for hospitals, clinics, healthtech startups, and healthcare professionals. Day\\-to\\-day responsibilities include designing social media creatives, presentations, brand assets, and marketing collateral; editing and animating videos; and ensuring design consistency across Stratist\u2019s verticals and client projects. The role also involves contributing to creative concepts, maintaining brand guidelines, preparing assets for different platforms and formats, and working closely with cross\\-functional stakeholders to meet timelines and quality standards.\n \n\n\n\n**Qualifications** \n\n\n\n* Strong graphic design skills, including experience in Graphics and Graphic Design for digital and print media.\n* Ability to develop visual identities using Logo Design and Branding for healthcare and professional services.\n* Proficiency in Typography and layout design to create clear, engaging, and accessible visual communication.\n* Hands\\-on experience with video editing and motion graphics software (e.g., Adobe Premiere Pro, After Effects, or equivalent).\n* Proficiency in industry\\-standard design tools such as Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, and related applications.\n* Understanding of digital marketing creatives, social media design formats, and content\\-driven visual storytelling.\n* Strong attention to detail, time management skills, and the ability to handle multiple projects in a fast\\-paced environment.\n* Portfolio demonstrating static and video design work; experience in healthcare or B2B services is an advantage.\n* Relevant diploma or degree in Graphic Design, Visual Communication, Multimedia, or a related field is preferred.\n\n\n Benefits\n \n \u25cf A creative role with\n **real purpose \\& people impact** \n\n\n\n\n \u25cf Work closely with founders, marketers \\& creative strategists\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Access to Stratist Academy upskilling sessions\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Transparent communication and an ethical work culture\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf \u20b925,000/month CTC\n \n\n\n\n \u25cf Office in\n **Jayanagar, Bangalore**","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467508652","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467508652"},{"title":"Media Consultant","company":"Prashanthi Balamandira Trust","location":"Karnataka","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468613133","source":"linkedin","experience":"8 Yrs","skills":[100,103,104],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**About the Company** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Sri Madhusudan Sai Global Humanitarian Mission passionately provides free Nutrition, Education, and Healthcare to those in need across more than 100 countries. Under the visionary leadership of the globally acclaimed humanitarian, Sadguru Sri Madhusudan Sai, the Organisation is dedicated to uplifting the most marginalised communities. The mission is grounded in the ethos of selfless service, guided by the belief that all are a part of \u2018One World, One Family\u2019.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**About the Role** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Join our dynamic team as a Media Consultant, where you will spearhead our PR and media initiatives, driving awareness and support for our impactful causes. This role offers a unique opportunity to utilise your expertise in media strategy, forge partnerships with key stakeholders, and leverage various platforms to amplify the organisation\u2019s message and mission.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Responsibilities** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* Develop and implement comprehensive media strategies to enhance brand visibility and support organisational objectives.\n* Cultivate relationships with editors, journalists, and news channels to secure coverage and promote the organisation\u2019s initiatives.\n* Pitch compelling story ideas and press releases to secure positive coverage of organisation's initiatives, events, and milestones.\n* Monitor media coverage and industry trends to identify opportunities for strategic engagement and proactive outreach.\n* Collaborate cross\\-functionally with internal teams to ensure alignment of messaging and maximise media impact.\n* Provide media training and support to spokespeople and staff members as needed.\n* Develop and implement crisis communication plans to effectively manage and mitigate reputational risks in the event of negative media coverage or emergencies.\n* Track and analyse media metrics to measure the effectiveness of PR efforts and inform future strategies.\n* Stay abreast of emerging technologies and platforms to innovate media tactics and maintain relevance in a rapidly evolving landscape.\n* Develop and manage the annual media budget, allocating resources strategically to maximise ROI and achieve organisational goals.\n* Track expenditures and performance against budget targets, providing regular updates and recommendations for adjustments as needed.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Qualifications** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* Bachelor's degree in Communications, Journalism, Public Relations, or a related field; Master's degree preferred.\n* Proven experience of 6\\-8 years in media relations, PR, or journalism, with a focus on strategic planning and execution.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Required Skills** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* Strong network of media contacts across print, broadcast, and digital platforms.\n* Exceptional written and verbal communication skills.\n* Demonstrated success in securing media coverage and generating positive publicity for organisations or causes.\n* Strategic thinker with a creative mindset and the ability to generate innovative ideas for media campaigns.\n* Excellent project management skills, with the ability to prioritise tasks, meet deadlines, and adapt to changing priorities.\n* Experience working in multicultural or international settings, with the ability to navigate cultural nuances and communicate effectively with diverse stakeholders.\n* Adherence to organisational policies and guidelines, including those related to media relations, privacy, and data protection.\n* Proficiency in media monitoring tools, analytics platforms, and Microsoft Office Suite.\n* Passion for social impact and a commitment to the organisation\u2019s mission and values.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Preferred Skills** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* None specified.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Pay range and compensation package** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n This is a full\\-time, work from office based role.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Equal Opportunity Statement** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Joining SMSGHM offers a chance to impact marginalised communities globally. With a focus on free Nutrition, Education, and Healthcare across more than 100 countries, your efforts directly contribute to positive change. Being part of our mission means experiencing the joy of helping others and knowing your contributions bring happiness to those in need.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468613133","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468613133"},{"title":"Performance Marketer","company":"Reev Travels","location":"Bangalore","date_posted":"2026-09-16","url":"https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=709055b46cacfb28&from=serp&vjs=3","source":"indeed","experience":"3 Yrs","skills":[103,105,107],"is_walkin":false,"description":"Performance Marketing Executive \u2013 Travel Industry\n\n**Location:** Bengaluru \\| **Type:** Full\\-Time\n\n**Key Responsibilities:**\n\n* Manage Google Ads, Meta Ads, and other digital campaigns.\n* Generate quality leads for holiday packages, visa, flights, and travel services.\n* Monitor and optimize CPL, conversions, ROI, and campaign performance.\n* Conduct audience and competitor research.\n* Create ad copies/creative campaigns and coordinate with the Sales team.\n* Track leads and prepare regular performance reports.\n\n**Requirements:**\n\n* 1\u20133 years of Performance Marketing experience.\n* Hands\\-on experience with Google Ads and Meta Ads.\n* Travel/Travel\\-tech industry experience preferred.\n* Strong analytical and communication skills.\n\nPay: \u20b9100,000\\.84 \\- \u20b9300,000\\.05 per month\n\nBenefits:\n\n* Health insurance\n* Paid sick time\n\nWork Location: In person","indeed_jk":"709055b46cacfb28","permanent_url":"https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=709055b46cacfb28&from=serp&vjs=3"},{"title":"Brand Development Specialist","company":"trueceil","location":"Kochi","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467528763","source":"linkedin","experience":"5 Yrs","skills":[103,106,107],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**BRAND DEVELOPMENT SPECIALIST** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**trueceil\u2122 \\|** \n Built Above Standard\n \n\n\n\n**Location:** \n Kochi, Kerala\n \n\n\n\n**Employment Type:** \n Full\\-Time\n \n\n\n\n**Experience:** \n 2\u20135 Years\n \n\n\n\n**Industry:** \n Architectural Products \\| Building Materials \\| Interior Systems\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**About trueceil\u2122** \n\n\n\n\n**trueceil\u2122** \n is an emerging architectural ceiling systems brand offering\n **design\\-led, reliable metal ceiling solutions** \n for commercial, institutional and architectural spaces.\n \n\n\n\n Our portfolio includes\n **metal ceiling tiles, lay\\-in, clip\\-in, open\\-cell, baffles, linear ceilings and grid systems.** \n\n\n\n\n**As trueceil continues to grow, we are looking for a Brand Development Specialist** \n to strengthen our presence across the architecture, interiors and construction industry.\n \n\n\n\n This is an opportunity to contribute directly to the\n **growth, visibility and market development of an emerging brand.** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**The Role** \n\n\n\n\n You will play a key role in developing trueceil's\n **brand presence, professional network and business opportunities.** \n\n\n\n\n**Working closely with management, you will identify new opportunities, build relationships with industry professionals, increase brand visibility and develop a strong project pipeline.** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Key Responsibilities** \n\n\n\n\n Brand Development\n \n\n\n* Support trueceil's brand positioning and market development initiatives.\n* Develop opportunities to increase brand awareness and professional visibility.\n* Support product launches, exhibitions, events and marketing campaigns.\n* Coordinate with creative teams on presentations, catalogues, samples and brand communication.\n\n\n\n Architectural \\& Market Engagement\n \n\n\n* Build relationships with architects, interior designers, consultants, contractors and project teams.\n* Conduct product presentations, sample demonstrations and design discussions.\n* Identify upcoming projects and opportunities for TRUECEIL products to be considered or specified.\n* Develop and maintain a strong professional network.\n\n\n\n Project \\& Business Development\n \n\n\n* Identify new markets, customer segments and project opportunities.\n* Track projects from design and specification through tender and execution.\n* Coordinate with internal teams for samples, technical information and quotations.\n* Develop qualified business opportunities and support their conversion into projects.\n\n\n\n Market Intelligence\n \n\n\n* Monitor competitor products, pricing, positioning and market activity.\n* Track industry trends and gather feedback from customers and professionals.\n* Identify market gaps and opportunities and share insights with management.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**What We Are Looking For** \n\n\n\n\n We are looking for someone who is\n **proactive, commercially aware, articulate and relationship\\-driven.** \n\n\n\n* Strong communication and presentation skills.\n* Confidence interacting with architects, designers, consultants and business professionals.\n* Interest in architecture, interiors, construction or building products.\n* Strong networking and relationship\\-management abilities.\n* Ability to understand technical products and communicate their value.\n* Willingness to travel and work independently.\n* Ability to take ownership and create opportunities.\n\n\n\n**We Value People Who** \n :\n \n\n\n\n**Create opportunities. Build relationships. Think beyond the next sale. Take ownership.** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Experience** \n\n\n\n\n**2\u20135 years of relevant experience preferred.** \n\n\n\n\n**Experience in architectural products, building materials, interior products, ceiling systems, acoustics, construction or other B2B industries** \n will be an advantage.\n \n\n\n\n Experience working with\n **architects, designers, consultants or contractors** \n is particularly valuable.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Why Join trueceil?** \n\n\n\n\n trueceil is at an exciting stage of growth where\n **your work can directly influence the future of the brand.** \n\n\n\n\n**You will work closely with management and gain exposure to:** \n\n\n\n\n**Brand Development \\| Market Strategy \\| Architecture \\& Design \\| Business Development \\| Project Development \\| Product Marketing** \n\n\n\n\n**As trueceil grows, so will the opportunity for greater responsibility, ownership and career progression.** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Compensation** \n\n\n\n\n Compensation will be based on relevant experience and capabilities \\+ performance\\-based incentives\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Build The Next Stage Of trueceil\u2122** \n\n\n\n\n If you want to\n **build relationships, develop markets and play a meaningful role in growing an architectural brand** \n , we would like to hear from you.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**trueceil\u2122** \n\n\n\n\n Built Above Standard","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467528763","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467528763"},{"title":"District Account Manager - VELYS","company":"Johnson & Johnson MedTech","location":"Kochi","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468247237","source":"linkedin","experience":"Manager","skills":[103,105,106,107,114],"is_walkin":false,"description":"At Johnson \\& Johnson,\u202fwe believe health is everything. Our strength in healthcare innovation empowers us to build a\u202fworld where complex diseases are prevented, treated, and cured,\u202fwhere treatments are smarter and less invasive, and\u202fsolutions are personal.\u202fThrough our expertise in Innovative Medicine and MedTech, we are uniquely positioned to innovate across the full spectrum of healthcare solutions today to deliver the breakthroughs of tomorrow, and profoundly impact health for humanity.\u202fLearn more at jnj.com.\n   \n\n  \n\n As guided by Our Credo, Johnson \\& Johnson is responsible to our employees who work with us throughout the world. We provide an inclusive work environment where each person is considered as an individual. At Johnson \\& Johnson, we respect the diversity and dignity of our employees and recognize their merit.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Job Function**\n MedTech Sales\n   \n\n  \n\n**Job Sub Function**\n Clinical Sales \u2013 Surgeons (Commission)\n   \n\n  \n\n**Job Category**\n Professional\n   \n\n  \n\n**All Job Posting Locations:**\n Chennai, Tamil Nadu, India, Cochin, Kerala, India\n   \n\n  \n\n**Job Description**\n**About DePuy Synthes**\n At DePuy Synthes, we are transforming orthopaedic care through intelligent technologies, data\\-driven insights, and robotic\\-assisted surgery. As part of Johnson \\& Johnson MedTech, we are committed to advancing patient outcomes through innovation, education, and clinical excellence.\n   \n\n  \n\n This is an exciting opportunity to work with industry\\-leading robotic and digital surgery platforms, collaborate with renowned surgeons, and contribute to the adoption of next\\-generation surgical technologies. We provide world\\-class training, professional development, and a dynamic environment where high performers can build a rewarding career.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Position Summary**\n The District Account Manager \u2013 Digital Surgery is responsible for driving adoption and utilization of Digital Surgery solutions, including robotic\\-assisted surgery platforms, navigation technologies, and data\\-enabled surgical workflows within the assigned territory.\n   \n\n  \n\n The role focuses on executing surgeon conversion strategies, developing customer partnerships, supporting clinical excellence, and achieving sales and utilization targets. The District Account Manager will collaborate closely with Joint Reconstruction sales teams, marketing, clinical specialists, and hospital stakeholders to accelerate the adoption of Smart Surgery solutions.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Key Responsibilities**\n**Business Development \\& Sales Growth**\n* Drive sales growth and market expansion of Digital Surgery solutions within the assigned territory.\n* Develop and execute strategic account plans to increase adoption of robotic\\-assisted surgery technologies.\n* Identify, prioritize, and convert target surgeons, hospitals, and healthcare systems through structured conversion plans.\n* Achieve or exceed assigned sales, utilization, and market development targets.\n* Build a sustainable pipeline of opportunities and maintain accurate forecasting.\n\n\n**Surgeon Engagement \\& Customer Development**\n* Establish strong relationships with key orthopaedic surgeons, hospital administrators, theatre managers, and clinical teams.\n* Drive surgeon conversions through evidence\\-based discussions, clinical value propositions, and workflow optimization.\n* Support surgeon onboarding and adoption programs to ensure successful technology implementation.\n* Act as a trusted advisor to customers by demonstrating clinical, operational, and economic value.\n\n\n**Clinical \\& Technical Support**\n* Provide in\\-theatre support during robotic\\-assisted procedures and technology\\-enabled surgeries.\n* Deliver product demonstrations, workshops, and educational programs for surgeons and operating room staff.\n* Ensure customers are trained and confident in the utilization of Digital Surgery technologies.\n* Collaborate with Clinical Specialists to maximize utilization and customer satisfaction.\n\n\n**Strategic Account Management**\n* Develop territory business plans aligned with regional and national objectives.\n* Monitor competitive activities, market trends, and customer needs to identify growth opportunities.\n* Drive capital equipment opportunities through effective stakeholder engagement and value\\-based selling.\n* Support contract negotiations, business reviews, and technology utilization assessments.\n\n\n**Cross\\-functional Collaboration**\n* Partner closely with Joint Reconstruction Sales, Marketing, Clinical Education, Professional Education, and Service teams.\n* Support product launches, customer education initiatives, and strategic marketing programs.\n* Contribute to best\\-practice sharing and continuous improvement initiatives across the Digital Surgery business.\n\n\n**Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)**\n* Achievement of Digital Surgery sales targets.\n* Surgeon conversion and adoption metrics.\n* Robotic utilization growth.\n* New account acquisition and account penetration.\n* Customer satisfaction and retention.\n* Market share growth within assigned territory.\n* Training and education program effectiveness.\n* Forecast accuracy and pipeline development.\n\n\n**Essential**\n**Qualifications \\& Experience**\n* Bachelor's degree in Life Sciences, Biomedical Engineering, Physiotherapy, Healthcare, Business, or related discipline.\n* Demonstrated success in medical device, healthcare technology, orthopaedics, or capital equipment sales.\n* Strong presentation, negotiation, and relationship management skills.\n* Ability to work effectively in a fast\\-paced and highly technical environment.\n* Strong business acumen and analytical mindset.\n* Excellent verbal and written communication skills.\n\n\n**Preferred**\n* Experience in Orthopaedics, Joint Reconstruction, Surgical Navigation, Robotics, Digital Health, or Operating Theatre environments.\n* Experience supporting surgeons during surgical procedures.\n* Knowledge of robotic\\-assisted surgery technologies and healthcare digital transformation.\n* Experience influencing multiple stakeholders in complex hospital sales environments.\n\n\n**Desired Competencies**\n* Strategic Thinking\n* Customer Centricity\n* Commercial Excellence\n* Technical Aptitude\n* Clinical Credibility\n* Influencing \\& Negotiation Skills\n* Problem Solving\n* Collaboration \\& Teamwork\n* Adaptability and Resilience\n* Results Orientation\n\n\n**Required Skills**\n**Preferred Skills:**\n Account Management, Business Behavior, Collaboration, Cultural Competence, Customer Analytics, Customer Centricity, Execution Focus, Healthcare Trends, Issue Escalation, Market Knowledge, Market Research, Medical Technology, Sales, Sales Support, Solutions Selling, Sustainable Procurement, Vendor Selection","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468247237","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468247237"},{"title":"Growth & Revenue Lead (AI Tech)","company":"Tuck - Virtual Try On","location":"Kochi","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467140812","source":"linkedin","experience":"3 Yrs","skills":[7,102,103,104,105],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**Job description:** \n\n\n\n\n The Opportunity You already know how to sell technology. You know how to open a conversation, navigate objections, and close deals. But you might be missing two things: a product that genuinely disrupts its category, and a compensation structure where your effort compounds instead of resetting to zero every quarter.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n We are a fast\\-growing, highly agile deeptech company looking for a seasoned sales professional to build and scale our outbound sales function. You won't just be executing someone else's playbook; you will be helping to write it.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**What We Do** \n\n\n\n\n Tuck is an AI\\-powered virtual try\\-on platform for global e\\-commerce apparel brands. We solve a fundamental problem: shoppers hesitate to buy when they can't visualize the fit, leading to abandoned carts and high return rates. Tuck allows shoppers to see garments on their own photos, matched perfectly with brand size charts, directly driving up merchant conversions.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Unlike competitors using off\\-the\\-shelf AI wrappers, we built a proprietary pipeline that delivers unmatched realism on actual retail catalogs. Our leadership team has a proven track record of building category\\-defining technology, having previously built India\u2019s first cashierless store technology which was successfully acquired by Amazon.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n The Role Your focus will be entirely on selling Tuck to founders and e\\-commerce heads of D2C fashion brands globally. You will open conversations, diagnose their store's bottlenecks, demonstrate our solution using their own product catalogs, and close deals.\n \n\n\n\n*Crucially: You won\u2019t spend your days hunting for leads.* \n We provide a researched, qualified pipeline. Your job is to drive the conversation. You will also have a seat at the table to shape our pitch, target segments, and go\\-to\\-market strategy.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**The Compensation** \n\n\n\n* **Fixed Base:** \n \u20b940,000 \u2013 \u20b960,000 monthly, commensurate with experience.\n* **Closing Incentives:** \n Uncapped per\\-client bonuses scaled to the plan they choose.\n* **Recurring Commission:** \n 5% of your client's monthly subscription fee for their first 12 months. Your income grows with your book of business.\n* **Target Earnings:** \n Realistic OTE (On\\-Target Earnings) for a strong performer is\n **\u20b91,00,000 \u2013 \u20b91,25,000/month** \n , scaling higher as your recurring portfolio builds.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Who We're Looking For** \n\n\n\n* **Experience:** \n Minimum 3 years in B2B technology sales (SaaS, software, or IT products).\n* **Communication:** \n Exceptional, confident spoken English. You must be comfortable speaking peer\\-to\\-peer with global founders.\n* **Business Acumen:** \n A deep curiosity about business metrics. You should be able to intelligently discuss Customer Acquisition Cost (CAC), conversion rates, return logistics, and profit margins\u2014not just recite software features.\n* **Resilience:** \n Comfortable owning a revenue target, managing a pipeline, and navigating the reality of B2B sales.\n* *Advantageous:* \n Familiarity with Shopify/e\\-commerce ecosystems, strong CRM discipline, and experience in international markets.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**What to Expect** \n\n\n\n\n You will work directly with the founders, receiving hands\\-on product training from day one. You are joining early enough that whoever successfully builds this function will eventually lead it.\n \n\n\n\n We value transparency: building a solid client base takes time, and we maintain a clear performance bar for the first three months, which will be transparently discussed prior to an offer. We offer a dynamic environment where you experience real ownership rather than just acting as a cog in an existing machine.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**How We Hire** \n\n\n\n\n Shortlisted candidates will be invited to a live mock sales call (product details will be provided in advance).","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467140812","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467140812"},{"title":"Immigration Consultant","company":"CanApprove Consultancy Services","location":"Kochi","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467511586","source":"linkedin","skills":[103,105],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**Company Description** \n CanApprove is a globally recognized immigration and education consultancy with a presence across multiple countries and over two decades of industry experience. The organization provides a wide range of professional services, including immigration support, overseas education guidance, and legal consultation. CanApprove focuses on delivering structured, reliable advice to individuals seeking opportunities abroad. The company regularly conducts open forums and virtual events, such as its Fly Canada initiatives, to provide transparent information and engage with prospective clients.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Role Description** \n\n\n\n\n This is a full\\-time, on\\-site Sales Consultant \u2013 Immigration role based in Kochi. The Sales Consultant will guide prospective clients through immigration options, explain processes and eligibility, and recommend suitable programs based on individual profiles. Daily responsibilities include conducting consultations, responding to inquiries, preparing and presenting service proposals, and following up with leads to support conversions. The role involves maintaining accurate client records, coordinating with internal teams to ensure smooth service delivery, and achieving set sales and performance targets. The Sales Consultant will also contribute to client satisfaction by providing clear communication, timely updates, and professional support throughout the consultation journey.\n \n\n\n\n**Qualifications** \n\n\n\n* Strong Sales Consulting and Consulting skills to assess client needs and recommend appropriate immigration solutions.\n* Customer Satisfaction and Customer Service skills to build trust, manage expectations, and maintain long\\-term relationships.\n* Excellent Communication skills, to explain complex immigration processes clearly and confidently.\n* Ability to work with targets, prioritize tasks, and manage time effectively in a fast\\-paced consultancy environment.\n* Strong willingness to learn new products and client management tools.\n* Prior experience in immigration, overseas education, or related consulting roles is an advantage.\n* Bachelor\u2019s degree in any discipline; additional certifications in sales or immigration consulting are a plus.\n* Professional demeanor, ethical approach, and commitment to providing non\\-discriminatory, client\\-focused service.\n\n\n\n**Vacancies Available At** \n\n\n\n* Kochi \\- 5\n* Angamali \\- 3\n* Thiruvalla \\- 6\n* Thrissur \\- 5\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Interested candidates can WhatsApp your resume to \\+91 7994490888 or mail to recruiter@canapprove.com","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467511586","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467511586"},{"title":"Account Manager- Supervising Associate","company":"EY","location":"Kochi","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4457482339","source":"linkedin","experience":"Manager","skills":[31,32,33,43,100,103,104,105,106,107,110],"is_walkin":false,"description":"At EY, you\u2019ll have the chance to build a career as unique as you are, with the global scale, support, inclusive culture and technology to become the best version of you. And we\u2019re counting on your unique voice and perspective to help EY become even better, too. Join us and build an exceptional experience for yourself, and a better working world for all.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Job Description**\n**Job Title:**\n Account Manager\n   \n\n  \n\n Function:\n   \n\n  \n\n Markets\n   \n\n  \n\n Skill Level:\n   \n\n  \n\n**Sub Function:**\n Account Activation\n   \n\n  \n\n**The opportunity**\n The Account Manager in GDS is primarily responsible to work with the with account leadership to support the planning and implementation of the account activation strategy. The GDS AM will closely work with the Global Client Service Partner (GCSP) and Client Executive (CE) to drive global account activation; drive account management excellence; sales and program management; and account communications \\& administration and will perform all the activities that doesn\u2019t require client proximity. He / She ensures that all locations and Service Lines (SL) of the firm are actively engaged around our global accounts and that we deliver Exceptional Client Service (ECS) in all internal and external encounters. This role will be aligned to GCSP / CE / account team and will be based in a non\\-client proximate location\n   \n\n  \n\n**Your Key Responsibilities**\n**Account Management \\& Acceleration Support:**\n* Implement Global BD strategy, methodology and processes at Account level\n* Co\\-develop account strategy working with account leadership and drive global execution of account plan\n* Support the account team in driving service line planning activity and account integration\n* Responsible to conduct Account Maturity Assessments and supports in preparation of Account Acceleration sessions\n* Prepare the global account meeting materials and facilitate account team meetings\n* Responsible for follow\\-up on account actions by tracking progress against deadlines and driving activity\n* Understand both the client\u2019s business agenda and EY services to enable leveraging the global EY network to connect our clients to the right people\n* Develop and manage the account onboarding process and appropriate materials\n* Co\\-develop client experience program, drive execution to collate client feedbacks and follow\\-up action plan\n* Act as a project manager for Account specific initiatives/projects\n* Review of account financials to provide awareness to account leadership on drivers of account performance\n* Monitoring of operational metrics important to team each month and working with account partners or service line leaders on troubleshooting issues\n* Support special projects as needed that require financial data/analysis\n\n\n**Sales and Program Management:**\n* Manage the annual global revenue planning process with the with service leaders on EY\u2019s priority accounts\n* Own and manage the Client Relationship Management (CRM) process\n* Co\\-develop the account relationship strategy, including management of the global relationship map\n* Manage the account pipeline process and drive discipline across global team\n* Coordinate the pursuit process for opportunities, working closely with key partners\n* Execute win/loss debriefs\n* Identify EY thought leadership and insights to be shared with the client\n* Creation and maintenance of account marketing materials (i.e. team brochure discussion relationship history, or Value Scorecard or procurement showcase doc)\n* Develop and maintain relationship of Account Managers, Market Segment Managers, to understand latest market\\- place, alliance, and solution activity within sector or like accounts\n\n\n**Information and Knowledge Management**\n* Be strategic to collaborate and partner with enabling functions of EY in supporting the account (where applicable):\n* Offshore Account Enablement team in India \u2013 pipeline management, financial analysis, sales cycle support, client research, Account plan management\n* EY Knowledge \u2013 Account Analysis, Quarterly earnings call summaries, travel packs on client\u2019s business, competitive landscape\n* Finance \u2013 Any financial needs of the account\n* Brand, Marketing and Communications \u2013 Account specific events, targeted thought leadership\n* Administrative Support \u2013 Meeting scheduling and any other administrative tasks\n* Global Sector/Industry \u2013 Identify market trends and EY insights\n* Service lines and geographies \\- Create process flows required for the team to capture information across account\n* Build and manage a repository of team information (i.e. MSA, Rate Card, SOW templates, onboarding documents, team process documents, qualifications, etc) and guide team on how to access and use\n* Develop and maintain relationships with the account teams to understand best practices for team information and knowledge management\n\n\n**Marketing Management**\n* Development and execution of account marketing plan to include\n* Distribution of thought leadership and/or event invites to relationships targets\n* Alumni relations\n* Support creation and distribution of team communications (i.e. team/client newsletter, WIN announcements)\n* Develop and maintain relationships with account teams to understand best practices for marketing activities\n\n\n**Communications and Administration**\n* Serves as subject matter expert for all information related to the account\n* Leverage EY resources to support the account\n* In consultation with account leadership manages Account specific events, identifies and leverages targeted thought leadership\n* Global Sector/Industry \\- Identify market trends and EY insights to take to account\n* Serve as the knowledge steward of the account and with the assistance of EY Knowledge, connect global team to EY tools and client business issues\n\n\n**Analytical/Decision Making Responsibilities:**\n* May be required to make decisions on behalf of Partners to expedite results\n* Influences without direct authority, frequently providing coaching and input to a high level of firm leadership\n\n\n**Skills And Attributes For Success**\n* Project Management \u2013 experience building and managing project plans\n* Presentation/Analysis \u2013 experience building .ppt presentations or discussion documents to explain a strategy, process, or relationship history; experience using .xls to analyze data for generating insights on trends within data set\n* Professional maturity to confidently interact with Account leaders. Demonstrate a level of assertiveness, and authority while communicating with the Senior Stakeholders and ability to articulate the viewpoints in a succinct manner\n* Communication \u2013 Demonstrate effective communication at all levels of the organization. Understand the nuances, ability to listen effectively, have a global mindset to operate effectively across borders\n* Consultative \u2013 demonstrate ability to approach problems and/or projects through effective question/answer techniques to identify needs/issues/desired outcomes and propose solutions to meet needs/issues/desired outcomes\n* Emotional Intelligence \u2013 demonstrate understanding of different working/personality styles and appreciation of need to flex approach and message to effectively engage\n* Networking \u2013 demonstrate ability to create networks within a company and use it to navigate across an organization of getting information to answer questions that arise across account\n* Entrepreneur/Proactive behaviors \u2013 desire to make the role their own and to create opportunity areas to involve themselves in day\\-to\\-day operations\n\n\n**Good to have**\n* People management \u2013 Effectively leading, mentoring and communicating with individual/team to achieve common goal\n\n\n**To qualify for the role, you must have**\n* Postgraduate in business management \u2013 preferably an MBA\n* 8\\+ years working in a professional services firm delivering operational enablement service to teams in different geographies plus previous sales, marketing, business development experience would be preferable\n\n\n**Certification Requirements**\n* Expected to remain current on relevant EY training and curriculum (e.g., Account Management Framework (AMF), Lead Badges, among others\n\n\n**Ideally, you\u2019ll also have**\n* Account Management and data reporting skills\n* Exposure to tools like Tableau, PowerBi etc\n* Credible experience working in a fast\\-moving, client\\-driven environment\n\n\n**Technologies and Tools**\n**Must Haves**\n Mastery of the Microsoft Suite (Outlook, Skype, Excel, PowerPoint, Word, SharePoint) \\& Data Visualization\n   \n\n  \n\n**Nice to Have**\n* Experience using Procurement portals (i.e. SAP Fieldglass, Ariba, Coupa, and Beeline)\n* Microsoft BI\n* Exposure to AI\\-enabled platforms\n\n\n**What We Look For**\n* A Team of people with commercial acumen, technical experience, and enthusiasm to learn new things in this fast\\-moving environment\n* A professional with strong interpersonal skills \\- confidence, maturity \\& ability to build strong client relationships\n\n\n**What We Offer**\n EY Global Delivery Services (GDS) is a dynamic and truly global delivery network. We work across six locations \u2013 Argentina, China, India, the Philippines, Poland, and the UK \u2013 and with teams from all EY service lines, geographies, and sectors, playing a vital role in the delivery of the EY growth strategy. From accountants to coders to advisory consultants, we offer a wide variety of fulfilling career opportunities that span all business disciplines. In GDS, you will collaborate with EY teams on exciting projects and work with well\\-known brands from across the globe. We\u2019ll introduce you to an ever\\-expanding ecosystem of people, learning, skills, and insights that will stay with you throughout your career.\n   \n\n  \n\n* Continuous learning: You\u2019ll develop the mindset and skills to navigate whatever comes next.\n* Success, as defined by you: We\u2019ll provide the tools and flexibility, so you can make a meaningful impact, your way.\n* Transformative leadership: We\u2019ll give you the insights, coaching and confidence to be the leader the world needs.\n* Diverse and inclusive culture: You\u2019ll be embraced for who you are and empowered to use your voice to help others find theirs.\n\n\n**EY \\| Building a better working world**\n EY exists to build a better working world, helping to create long\\-term value for clients, people and society and build trust in the capital markets.\n   \n\n  \n\n Enabled by data and technology, diverse EY teams in over 150 countries provide trust through assurance and help clients grow, transform and operate.\n   \n\n  \n\n Working across assurance, consulting, law, strategy, tax and transactions, EY teams ask better questions to find new answers for the complex issues facing our world today.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4457482339","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4457482339"},{"title":"Travel Advisor","company":"TravelXpin","location":"Kochi","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466262143","source":"linkedin","skills":[105],"is_walkin":false,"description":"Job Location: Cochin\n \n\n\n\n Package offered : 25000 per month\n \n\n\n\n**Role Description** \n\n\n\n\n Handle customer inquiries for\n **air tickets, hotels, holiday packages, transfers, travel insurance, and other travel services** \n .\n \n\n\n\n Understand customer requirements and recommend suitable travel options based on budget and preferences.\n \n\n\n\n Search and compare airline fares, schedules, baggage allowances, and applicable conditions.\n \n\n\n\n Prepare and share professional travel quotations with customers.\n \n\n\n\n Make and manage flight, hotel, and other travel reservations.\n \n\n\n\n Follow up with customers on quotations and convert inquiries into confirmed bookings.\n \n\n\n\n Maintain strong relationships with existing customers and develop new business opportunities.\n \n\n\n\n Handle ticketing, re\\-issuance, cancellations, refunds, and schedule changes as required.\n \n\n\n\n Provide customers with accurate information regarding travel documents, visa requirements, baggage rules, and airline policies.\n \n\n\n\n Ensure all bookings and customer information are accurately recorded in the company's systems.\n \n\n\n\n Monitor pending bookings, payments, ticketing deadlines, and booking confirmations.\n \n\n\n\n Handle customer complaints and provide timely solutions.\n \n\n\n\n Achieve individual and team\n **sales targets and revenue objectives** \n .\n \n\n\n\n Identify opportunities for upselling and cross\\-selling travel products and services.\n \n\n\n\n Keep updated with airline promotions, special fares, destination information, and travel industry developments.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466262143","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466262143"},{"title":"ServiceNow-Senior Manager","company":"EY","location":"Kochi","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4456922329","source":"linkedin","experience":"15-20 Yrs","skills":[7,100,102,104,105,106,112],"is_walkin":false,"description":"At EY, we\u2019re all in to shape your future with confidence.\n   \n\n  \n\n We\u2019ll help you succeed in a globally connected powerhouse of diverse teams and take your career wherever you want it to go.\n   \n\n  \n\n Join EY and help to build a better working world.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Service Now Associate Director**\n**Education Level**\n* High School Diploma/GED, Technical Diploma, Associate\u2019s Degree/College Diploma, Non\\-Degree Program, Bachelor\u2019s Degree, Master\u2019s Degree, Doctorate Degree, Higher Degree, Other\n* Bachelor\u2019s or Masters\n\n\n**Job Purpose**\n The incumbent should be able to lead a group in Service Now Practice and provide directions and strategies to growing the firm\u2019s Service Now footprint managing large and complex Service Now implementation, product development and sales enablement. This is a global role and candidate should have experience in working with large global teams spread across multiple geographies\n   \n\n  \n\n**Responsibilities, Qualifications, Certifications \\- External**\n**Requirements (including experience, skills and additional qualifications)**\n**Technical Skills Requirements**\n* Lead sales and pre\\-sales work in Service Now, respond to client proposals, participate in orals and help growing Service Now business\n* Should have in\\-depth knowledge and understanding of Service Now Partner ecosystem, licensing model and platform management models.\n* Capable in designing and developing large solutions combining Service Now platform, automation and workflow capabilities for EY cusotmers\n* Lead offshore team in all the Service Now modules like ITSM, ITOM, ITBM, HRSD, Sec Ops. The role will spread across blueprint, design, configuration, build and roll out phase.\n* The role involves knowledge and experience of both functional and technical aspect for a successful implementation, working closely with various stakeholders like business, process leads and offshore team.\n* Propose and deliver projects as per the agreed objectives to EY customers and/or to internal EY stakeholders\n* Build strong internal relationships within the firm and with other services across the organization\n* Develop people through effectively supervising, coaching, and mentoring staff. Conduct performance reviews and contribute to performance feedback for staff\n* Contribute to people\\-related initiatives including recruiting, retaining and training.\n* Maintain an educational program to continually develop personal skills of all staff\n* Perform an appropriate role in business development in terms of pre sales and practice development. for example, pre sales, internal engagement and / or knowledge management\n* 15 to 20 years of relevant experience, preferably from a top tier Global System Integrator\n\n\n**Additional Skills Requirements**\n* At least two Service Now Implementation Certifications\n* ITIL Intermediate, COBIT and or TOGAF certifications\n* Agile and scrum master certifications\n* PMP certification\n\n\n**EY \\| Building a better working world**\n EY is building a better working world by creating new value for clients, people, society and the planet, while building trust in capital markets.\n   \n\n  \n\n Enabled by data, AI and advanced technology, EY teams help clients shape the future with confidence and develop answers for the most pressing issues of today and tomorrow.\n   \n\n  \n\n EY teams work across a full spectrum of services in assurance, consulting, tax, strategy and transactions. Fueled by sector insights, a globally connected, multi\\-disciplinary network and diverse ecosystem partners, EY teams can provide services in more than 150 countries and territories.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4456922329","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4456922329"},{"title":"SAP Retail - Senior","company":"EY","location":"Kochi","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428285536","source":"linkedin","experience":"3 Yrs","skills":[7,43,102,104,105],"is_walkin":false,"description":"At EY, we\u2019re all in to shape your future with confidence.\n   \n\n  \n\n We\u2019ll help you succeed in a globally connected powerhouse of diverse teams and take your career wherever you want it to go.\n   \n\n  \n\n Join EY and help to build a better working world.\n   \n\n  \n\n**SAP Retail Senior**\n* Minimum 3 years of experience in SAP Retail / CAR design and configuration for digital and retail channels and POS integration.\n* Experience of at least 3\\-4 end\\-to\\-end full cycle implementations (from blueprinting, realisation, go live to production support) of S/4HANA Greenfield / Migration projects in the complex landscape as Team Lead.\n* Should have excellent configuration and training skills in the areas of implementation and support of the CAR\\-POSDTA, Multichannel and Inventory Visibility.\n* Should have experience in SAP IS\\-Retail and Store Operations. Fashion Management processes\n* Should have used consulting skills, business knowledge, and pre\\-configured solutions expertise to effectively integrate packaged technology into the client\u2019s business environment to achieve the client expected business results. Cross module (FI, SD, MM.) integration knowledge.\n* Proven Experience Designing And Implementing SAP IS Retail Programs, Including Organizational Structure, Master Data, Core Business processes, Data distribution, retail merchandise management, and integration to POS system.\n* Should have supported pre\\-sales engagements and phase 0 assessments.\n* Perform a deep study of complicated business process needs and recommend suitable system solutions; identify, analyse, validate, and document client requirements.\n* Conduct workshops to gather business requirements.\n* Map the business requirements, procedures, and objectives of the client; design the required product improvements to meet the client's demands.\n* Design, customise, configure, and test SAP IS\\-Retail.\n\n\n**Required Technical And Professional Expertise**\n* At least 3\\-7 years of work experience in SAP Retail or related retail consulting services engagements or business settings, implementing or using Retail business processes and systems is required.\n* Proven Experience of at least 3\\-4 end\\-to\\-end full cycle implementations (from blueprinting, realisation, go live to production support) of S/4HANA Greenfield / Migration projects in the complex landscape as Team Lead or Retail SME or Solution Architect.\n* Should have supported pre\\-sales engagements, including preparing and delivering customer presentations.\n* Must have extensive knowledge of SAP IS\\-Retail processes such as promotion management, distribution planning, retail pricing, and merchandise management.\n* Capability to assist in every phase of the SAP Retail implementation project.\n* Extensive comprehension of Retail business operations\n* Understanding SAP SD, MM, FI, and CAR module interface points.\n* The candidate must have experience with SAP S/4 HANA projects.\n* Capability to multitask and concurrently handle several deliverables and projects.\n* Capability to work in a team atmosphere and engage with people effectively.\n* Capability to effectively convey ideas and generate innovative solutions for challenging scenarios or situations within the Retail business industry.\n* Have sound knowledge of Materials Management and Sales and Distribution process\n* Configuration Knowledge of Available to Promise (ATP) \\& AATP, Promotion Management \\& Analysis, Ship from Store, Drop Shipping\n* Should have Strong integration experience with POS and e\\-Commerce applications\n* Extensive SAP Retail design and implementation experience\n* Experience with Fiori applications is a plus\n* Experience working in an Agile environment is desired\n* Experienced in implementation and rollout experience in either IS\\-Retail and S/4 Fashion projects\n\n\n**EY \\| Building a better working world**\n EY is building a better working world by creating new value for clients, people, society and the planet, while building trust in capital markets.\n   \n\n  \n\n Enabled by data, AI and advanced technology, EY teams help clients shape the future with confidence and develop answers for the most pressing issues of today and tomorrow.\n   \n\n  \n\n EY teams work across a full spectrum of services in assurance, consulting, tax, strategy and transactions. Fueled by sector insights, a globally connected, multi\\-disciplinary network and diverse ecosystem partners, EY teams can provide services in more than 150 countries and territories.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428285536","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428285536"},{"title":"Microsoft-CRM Technical-Senior Manager","company":"EY","location":"Kochi","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466204089","source":"linkedin","experience":"Senior","skills":[7,14,15,33,101,102,103,104,105,106,107,111,112,115,116],"is_walkin":false,"description":"At EY, you\u2019ll have the chance to build a career as unique as you are, with the global scale, support, inclusive culture and technology to become the best version of you. And we\u2019re counting on your unique voice and perspective to help EY become even better, too. Join us and build an exceptional experience for yourself, and a better working world for all.\n   \n\n  \n\n**AI Business Solutions \u2013 Dynamics CRM Technical Senior Manager Specialized:**\n At EY, we\u2019re all in to shape your future with confidence.\n   \n\n  \n\n We\u2019ll help you succeed in a globally connected powerhouse of diverse teams and take your career wherever you want it to go.\n   \n\n  \n\n Join EY and help to build a better working world.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About Global Delivery Services**\n Global Delivery Services refers to EY's worldwide network of service delivery centers. The GDS team plays an important role in EY\u2019s strategy by ensuring effective support to EY\u2019s growth agenda.\n   \n\n  \n\n Our journey started in 2002 with approximately 200 people. Today we stand at 80,000\\+ professionals in ten locations around the world. We operate in Argentina, China, Hungary, India, Philippines, Poland, Sri Lanka, Mexico, Spain and the United Kingdom.\n   \n\n  \n\n Client service is focused on providing Consulting, Assurance, Tax, Strategy \\& Transactions, and Knowledge support to our clients around the world. The teams enable account teams worldwide to provide seamless, high\\-quality, value\\-added support, helping deliver exceptional client service.\n   \n\n  \n\n Enablement Services provides cost\\-effective, high\\-skilled, and innovative services to support EY\u2019s global and local enablement teams. Markets, BMC, AWS, Finance and Accounting, Risk Management, Procurement, People Shared Services, IT Service Delivery and IT Global Infrastructure services, are among the services offered by Enablement Services.\n   \n\n  \n\n Our innovation specialists serve the GDS Client Service and Enablement Services teams, along with Service Lines, Core Business Services and Sectors. The team brings the desired environment, technologies and skilled teams together for facilitation, rapid prototyping and innovative thinking. The competencies offered include analytics, digital, user experience, mobile technology, infrastructure, Microsoft technologies and open innovation.\n   \n\n  \n\n**The Opportunity**\n We are seeking an experienced MS CRM Technical Senior Manager to lead large\\-scale Dynamics 365 CRM engagements, drive solution excellence, and contribute to business growth. This role combines deep technical expertise with strategic leadership, ensuring successful delivery, stakeholder alignment, and expansion of CRM capabilities across accounts. You will play a key role in shaping solutions, mentoring teams, and driving business development initiatives within the Microsoft Business Applications ecosystem.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Your Key Responsibilities**\n* Lead end\\-to\\-end design and delivery of Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM solutions across complex programs.\n* Architect scalable, high\\-performance solutions aligned with business and technology strategies.\n* Drive solution quality, governance, and best practices across implementations.\n* Collaborate with stakeholders to define vision, roadmap, and transformation initiatives.\n* Provide technical leadership across multiple projects, ensuring adherence to timelines and budgets.\n* Mentor and guide teams, fostering a culture of innovation and continuous improvement.\n* Support pre\\-sales activities including solutioning, estimations, proposal development, and client presentations.\n* Identify and drive business development opportunities, including account growth, pipeline creation, and cross\\-sell of CRM and related capabilities.\n* Build strong client relationships and act as a trusted advisor for CRM transformations.\n* Ensure risk management, issue resolution, and proactive escalation across engagements.\n* Responsible for decision\\-making, optimizing processes, resource management, and overseeing team management as needed for task execution.\n* Accountable for allocating personnel, supervising team members, assigning tasks, ensuring that the team has the necessary tools and support to succeed in their roles and optimizing and evaluating their performance to meet organizational goals.\n\n\n**Skills And Attributes For Success**\n* Strong expertise in Microsoft Dynamics 365 (Sales, Customer Service, Marketing, etc.) and Power Platform.\n* Deep understanding of CRM architecture, customization, configuration, and extension capabilities.\n* Hands\\-on experience in integrations, data migration, and enterprise solution design.\n* Proven leadership in managing large, distributed teams and complex programs.\n* Strong stakeholder management, communication, and problem\\-solving skills.\n* Ability to balance technical delivery with business priorities and growth objectives.\n* Experience in Agile/DevOps methodologies and modern delivery practices.\n* Strong analytical mindset with focus on quality, scalability, and performance.\n\n\n**Ideally, you\u2019ll also**\n The following skills and experiences are preferred and will be considered an advantage:\n   \n\n  \n\n* Power Pages\n* Canvas Apps and Model\\-Driven Apps (Code Apps)\n* PCF (PowerApps Component Framework) Controls\n* Integrations using Azure Functions, Azure Logic Apps, and Azure Service Bus\n* Data Migration using SSIS (KingswaySoft) and Azure Data Factory\n* Copilot Studio\n* Dynamics 365 Project Operations\n* Dynamics 365 Field Service\n* Dynamics 365 Contact Center\n\n\n**What We Look For**\n* Bachelor\u2019s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field.\n* Total Experience: 12\\+ years\n* Relevant Experience: 12\\+ years\n* Proven track record of delivering Dynamics 365 CRM programs at scale.\n* Strong exposure to client\\-facing roles, including pre\\-sales and business development.\n* Experience working in global delivery models and cross\\-functional teams.\n* Bachelor\u2019s or Master\u2019s degree in engineering, Computer Science, or related field.\n* Relevant Microsoft certifications are preferred.\n\n\n**What We Offer You**\n At EY, we\u2019ll develop you with future\\-focused skills and equip you with world\\-class experiences. We\u2019ll empower you in a flexible environment, and fuel you and your extraordinary talents in a diverse and inclusive culture of globally connected teams. Learn more.\n   \n\n  \n\n Are you ready to shape your future with confidence? Apply today.\n   \n\n  \n\n To help create an equitable and inclusive experience during the recruitment process, please inform us as soon as possible about any disability\\-related adjustments or accommodations you may need.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Our Commitment:** \n As a commitment, we persistently endeavour to embody our values, fulfil our purpose, and champion inclusiveness. Our dedication is to cultivate EY into an environment where diverse perspectives are celebrated, creating a supportive atmosphere for individuals to authentically be themselves and contribute their utmost.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Professional Development:** \n From entry\\-level employees to senior leaders, we believe in continuous learning. We offer opportunities to build new skills, take on leadership roles, and connect and grow through mentorship.\n   \n\n  \n\n**People and Culture:** \n In our dynamic workplace, diversity, equity, and inclusiveness are ingrained in our culture. We're united by a commitment to create an environment where every individual's differences are valued, practices are equitable, fostering a sense of belonging. Our shared values include integrity, respect, teaming, inclusiveness, energy, enthusiasm, courage to lead, and building relationships based on doing the right thing.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Benefits:** \n Embark on a transformative career journey with us and indulge in a suite of premium benefits, encompassing exclusive health and wellness packages, enticing rewards, and cutting\\-edge learning opportunities that empower you to continually grow and excel in your professional and personal development.\n   \n\n  \n\n**How to Apply:** \n If you are passionate to join us and are aligned with our commitment to building a better working world, we invite you to apply by completing our user\\-friendly form with personal and professional information and by providing your consent to data privacy.\n   \n\n  \n\n Successful candidates advance to a competency\\-based interview. If mutual interest persists, a job offer awaits.\n   \n\n  \n\n \u201cWe are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to Diversity, Equity \\& Inclusion\u201d.\n   \n\n  \n\n**EY \\| Building a better working world**\n EY exists to build a better working world, helping to create long\\-term value for clients, people and society and build trust in the capital markets.\n   \n\n  \n\n Enabled by data and technology, diverse EY teams in over 150 countries provide trust through assurance and help clients grow, transform and operate.\n   \n\n  \n\n Working across assurance, consulting, law, strategy, tax and transactions, EY teams ask better questions to find new answers for the complex issues facing our world today.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466204089","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466204089"},{"title":"SCT_Tech Enablement_AI Architect_Manager","company":"EY","location":"Kochi","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467509113","source":"linkedin","skills":[1,7,12,14,15,16,17,18,30,33,35,103,104,111,112,116],"is_walkin":false,"description":"At EY, you\u2019ll have the chance to build a career as unique as you are, with the global scale, support, inclusive culture and technology to become the best version of you. And we\u2019re counting on your unique voice and perspective to help EY become even better, too. Join us and build an exceptional experience for yourself, and a better working world for all.\n   \n\n  \n\n**SCT\\-Tech Enablement \\- Manager**\n At EY, we\u2019re all in to shape your future with confidence.\n   \n\n  \n\n We\u2019ll help you succeed in a globally connected powerhouse of diverse teams and take your career wherever you want it to go.\n   \n\n  \n\n Join EY and help to build a better working world.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About Global Delivery Services**\n Global Delivery Services refers to EY's worldwide network of service delivery centers. The GDS team plays an important role in EY\u2019s strategy by ensuring effective support to EY\u2019s growth agenda.\n   \n\n  \n\n Our journey started in 2002 with approximately 200 people. Today we stand at 80,000\\+ professionals in ten locations around the world. We operate in Argentina, China, Hungary, India, Philippines, Poland, Sri Lanka, Mexico, Spain and the United Kingdom.\n   \n\n  \n\n Client service is focused on providing Consulting, Assurance, Tax, Strategy \\& Transactions, and Knowledge support to our clients around the world. The teams enable account teams worldwide to provide seamless, high\\-quality, value\\-added support, helping deliver exceptional client service.\n   \n\n  \n\n Enablement Services provides cost\\-effective, high\\-skilled, and innovative services to support EY\u2019s global and local enablement teams. Markets, BMC, AWS, Finance and Accounting, Risk Management, Procurement, People Shared Services, IT Service Delivery and IT Global Infrastructure services, are among the services offered by Enablement Services.\n   \n\n  \n\n Our innovation specialists serve the GDS Client Service and Enablement Services teams, along with Service Lines, Core Business Services and Sectors. The team brings the desired environment, technologies and skilled teams together for facilitation, rapid prototyping and innovative thinking. The competencies offered include analytics, digital, user experience, mobile technology, infrastructure, Microsoft technologies and open innovation.\n   \n\n  \n\n**The opportunity**\n AI Architect\\- SC products: We are seeking an experienced Supply Chain AI Solution Architect to join our Digital Supply Chain Team. This hybrid role combines enterprise AI architecture, Supply Chain taxonomies and knowledge graph, product thinking, and client advisory to translate business needs into secure, scalable solutions that deliver measurable value.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Your Key Responsibilities**\n* Collaborate with business stakeholders, product owners, and technical teams to identify AI opportunities and translate requirements into scalable AI solution architectures.\n* Design and architect enterprise\\-grade AI applications leveraging LLMs, RAG, Agentic AI, Knowledge Graphs, GraphRAG, and Multimodal AI patterns.\n* Define end\\-to\\-end AI solution architectures, including model selection, data retrieval strategy, orchestration frameworks, deployment models, and integration patterns.\n* Design and implement advanced prompting, context engineering, structured outputs, tool calling, workflow orchestration, and memory management strategies.\n* Architect hybrid retrieval solutions using vector search, semantic search, GraphRAG, SQL\\-based retrieval, and vectorless approaches.\n* Design and implement MCP\\-based integrations with enterprise applications, APIs, databases, and business systems.\n* Establish AI platform standards covering observability, evaluation frameworks, LLMOps, monitoring, governance, performance optimization, and cost management.\n* Define AI security architectures addressing prompt injection, data leakage, unauthorized tool access, jailbreak attempts, and AI\\-specific threats.\n* Ensure compliance with Responsible AI principles, privacy regulations, governance requirements, and security standards.\n* Conduct architecture reviews, technical assessments, proof\\-of\\-concepts, and production\\-readiness evaluations.\n* Drive AI adoption across business and technology teams through workshops, technical leadership, and stakeholder engagement.\n* Mentor AI engineers, architects, and developers while defining best practices, reusable frameworks, and reference architectures.\n* Stay current with emerging AI technologies, frameworks, and industry trends to drive continuous innovation.\n\n\n**To qualify for the role, you must have**\n* 12\\+ years of experience in software engineering, cloud architecture, data engineering, enterprise architecture, or related technology domains.\n* Strong experience designing and implementing enterprise AI, Generative AI, and intelligent automation solutions.\n* Hands\\-on experience with Large Language Models (LLMs), prompt engineering, context engineering, RAG, embeddings, reranking, and vector databases.\n* Strong knowledge of AI agent architectures, multi\\-agent systems, tool calling, memory strategies, and human\\-in\\-the\\-loop workflows.\n* Proficiency in Python, API development, microservices architecture, and distributed systems.\n* Experience with cloud platforms such as Microsoft Azure, AWS, or Google Cloud Platform and their AI services.\n* Strong understanding of databases, data platforms, event\\-driven architectures, and enterprise integration patterns.\n* Practical experience with MCP, REST APIs, JSON\\-RPC, OAuth, and secure integration frameworks.\n* Knowledge of AI evaluation frameworks, tracing, monitoring, observability, LLMOps, and AI cost optimization.\n* Understanding of model fine\\-tuning, LoRA/QLoRA, model routing, quantization, and inference optimization techniques.\n* Experience with multimodal AI, knowledge graphs, GraphRAG, SQL agents, and advanced retrieval architectures.\n* Excellent communication, stakeholder management, architecture documentation, and leadership skills.\n* Strong analytical and problem\\-solving capabilities with a focus on delivering business outcomes.\n\n\n**Ideally, you\u2019ll also have**\n* Experience with frameworks such as LangGraph, LangChain, LlamaIndex, Semantic Kernel, CrewAI, or equivalent orchestration platforms.\n* Experience working with OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini, Azure AI, AWS Bedrock, Hugging Face, or similar AI ecosystems.\n* Familiarity with vector databases and search platforms such as Pinecone, Qdrant, Weaviate, Milvus, pgvector, Elasticsearch, OpenSearch, or Neo4j.\n* Experience with Docker, Kubernetes, MLflow, vLLM, Langfuse, Ragas, DeepEval, and AI platform engineering practices.\n* Understanding of AI governance and security frameworks, including NIST AI RMF, OWASP GenAI Security, ISO/IEC 42001, and cloud security best practices.\n* Experience leading enterprise AI transformation initiatives, Centers of Excellence (CoE), or AI capability building programs.\n* Exposure to MLOps, DataOps, and enterprise deployment strategies for scalable AI solutions.\n* Experience engaging with executive stakeholders and presenting architecture roadmaps, AI strategies, and business cases.\n\n\n**What We Offer You**\n At EY, we\u2019ll develop you with future\\-focused skills and equip you with world\\-class experiences. We\u2019ll empower you in a flexible environment, and fuel you and your extraordinary talents in a diverse and inclusive culture of globally connected teams. Learn more.\n   \n\n  \n\n Are you ready to shape your future with confidence? Apply today.\n   \n\n  \n\n To help create an equitable and inclusive experience during the recruitment process, please inform us as soon as possible about any disability\\-related adjustments or accommodations you may need.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Our Commitment:** \n As a commitment, we persistently endeavour to embody our values, fulfil our purpose, and champion inclusiveness. Our dedication is to cultivate EY into an environment where diverse perspectives are celebrated, creating a supportive atmosphere for individuals to authentically be themselves and contribute their utmost.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Professional Development:** \n From entry\\-level employees to senior leaders, we believe in continuous learning. We offer opportunities to build new skills, take on leadership roles, and connect and grow through mentorship.\n   \n\n  \n\n**People and Culture:** \n In our dynamic workplace, diversity, equity, and inclusiveness are ingrained in our culture. We're united by a commitment to create an environment where every individual's differences are valued, practices are equitable, fostering a sense of belonging. Our shared values include integrity, respect, teaming, inclusiveness, energy, enthusiasm, courage to lead, and building relationships based on doing the right thing.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Benefits:** \n Embark on a transformative career journey with us and indulge in a suite of premium benefits, encompassing exclusive health and wellness packages, enticing rewards, and cutting\\-edge learning opportunities that empower you to continually grow and excel in your professional and personal development.\n   \n\n  \n\n**How to Apply:** \n If you are passionate to join us and are aligned with our commitment to building a better working world, we invite you to apply by completing our user\\-friendly form with personal and professional information and by providing your consent to data privacy.\n   \n\n  \n\n Successful candidates advance to a competency\\-based interview. If mutual interest persists, a job offer awaits.\n   \n\n  \n\n \u201cWe are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to Diversity, Equity \\& Inclusion\u201d.\n   \n\n  \n\n**EY \\| Building a better working world**\n EY exists to build a better working world, helping to create long\\-term value for clients, people and society and build trust in the capital markets.\n   \n\n  \n\n Enabled by data and technology, diverse EY teams in over 150 countries provide trust through assurance and help clients grow, transform and operate.\n   \n\n  \n\n Working across assurance, consulting, law, strategy, tax and transactions, EY teams ask better questions to find new answers for the complex issues facing our world today.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467509113","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4467509113"},{"title":"SAP TM-Senior","company":"EY","location":"Kochi","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4418759490","source":"linkedin","experience":"7 Yrs","skills":[7,14,33,41,43,103,104,105,111,112,116],"is_walkin":false,"description":"At EY, we\u2019re all in to shape your future with confidence.\n   \n\n  \n\n We\u2019ll help you succeed in a globally connected powerhouse of diverse teams and take your career wherever you want it to go.\n   \n\n  \n\n Join EY and help to build a better working world.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Advisory \u2013 SAP TM Functional Senior**\n At EY, we\u2019re all in to shape your future with confidence.\n   \n\n  \n\n We\u2019ll help you succeed in a globally connected powerhouse of diverse teams and take your career wherever you want it to go.\n   \n\n  \n\n Join EY and help to build a better working world.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About Global Delivery Services**\n Global Delivery Services refers to EY's worldwide network of service delivery centers. The GDS team plays an important role in EY\u2019s strategy by ensuring effective support to EY\u2019s growth agenda.\n   \n\n  \n\n Our journey started in 2002 with approximately 200 people. Today we stand at 80,000\\+ professionals in ten locations around the world. We operate in Argentina, China, Hungary, India, Philippines, Poland, Sri Lanka, Mexico, Spain and the United Kingdom.\n   \n\n  \n\n Client service is focused on providing Consulting, Assurance, Tax, Strategy \\& Transactions, and Knowledge support to our clients around the world. The teams enable account teams worldwide to provide seamless, high\\-quality, value\\-added support, helping deliver exceptional client service.\n   \n\n  \n\n Enablement Services provides cost\\-effective, high\\-skilled, and innovative services to support EY\u2019s global and local enablement teams. Markets, BMC, AWS, Finance and Accounting, Risk Management, Procurement, People Shared Services, IT Service Delivery and IT Global Infrastructure services, are among the services offered by Enablement Services.\n   \n\n  \n\n Our innovation specialists serve the GDS Client Service and Enablement Services teams, along with Service Lines, Core Business Services and Sectors. The team brings the desired environment, technologies and skilled teams together for facilitation, rapid prototyping and innovative thinking. The competencies offered include analytics, digital, user experience, mobile technology, infrastructure, Microsoft technologies and open innovation.\n   \n\n  \n\n**The Opportunity**\n The SAP TM Transportation Management Senior Consultant serves as a senior\\-level advisor responsible for leading complex SAP Transportation Management (TM) transformation initiatives for enterprise clients. This role combines deep SAP TM expertise with strategic consulting capabilities to design, implement, and optimize end\\-to\\-end transportation solutions that drive operational excellence, cost reduction, and supply chain visibility. The consultant participates in pursuing client sales opportunities and working on bid \\& proposal efforts along with activities including configuration and setting up the SAP TM system, assessment of client business problems, conducting the analysis to solve the problems, administration of engagement activities while contributing to practice growth and innovation.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Your Key Responsibilities**\n* Responsible for the successful delivery of the SAP TM module related deliverables in SAP and S4 HANA implementation, support, and upgrade projects to meet engagement objectives and budget\n* Lead design workshops with the client and responsible for requirement gathering, solution design, fit\\-gap analysis, writing functional specification, system configuration, testing and cutover activities for both standalone SAP TM system and embedded SAP TM in S/4 HANA\n* Design SAP TM system Integrations with other modules of SAP/S4 HANA (like EWM, SD, MM etc.) and 3rd Party system\n* Provide functional and business process expertise to the project team, resolve TM related client s issues and mentor junior team members\n* Handle various industry specific complex TM scenarios like shipper, LSP and carriers\n* Work with sales team, write proposals, define SAP TM scope and effort estimation for the new opportunities and present SAP TM capability to the potential client\n\n\n**Skills And Attributes For Success**\n**Technical and Professional Requirements:**\n* 5\\-7 years of experience in implementation, support and upgrade projects in SAP TM.\n* Must have good functional and business knowledge, worked in multiple E2E implementations, integration, testing and application support in S/4HANA embedded TM and SAP TM (latest versions)\n* Ability to interact with other cross functional teams from modules like OTC, EWM for integration scenario\n* Excellent written and verbal interpersonal skills for co\\-ordinating across teams\n* Should be able to lead workshop or working sessions with business\n* Knowledge in ABAP and debugging would be nice to have\n\n\n**Core SAP TM Competencies**\n* Comprehensive knowledge in all L3 aspects of SAP TM such as Order Management (Logistics Integration, Freight Unit, Forwarding Order, Freight Order, Freight Booking), Transportation Planning and Execution, Carrier Selection, Charge Calculation and Freight Settlement, Invoice Integration and Carrier Communication methodologies\n* Proficiency in Master Data setup such as Resource Management, Locations, Business Partners etc.\n* Deep understanding of SAP TM integration with SAP ERP S/4HANA logistics (SD, MM, LE) and embedded TM scenarios\n* Expertise in Transportation Planning strategies: manual planning, Transportation Cockpit, optimizer\\-based planning (VSR), and automated freight unit building\n* Proficiency in Freight Order Lifecycle Management, Freight Tendering processes, Subcontracting and Execution monitoring\n* Advanced knowledge of Charge calculation, Freight Agreement Management, Rate tables and Transportation cost allocation\n\n\n**Technical Skills**\n* SAP TM configuration and customizing across all functional areas (master data, organizational structures, profiles setup for Planning, business rules such as BRF\\+ conditions)\n* Data migration methodologies using DRF, LSMW, SAP Data Services, or Migration Cockpit; system landscape design (Development, Quality, Production)\n* Understanding of SAP TM on HANA optimization, performance tuning, and analytics capabilities\n* Expertise in implementation planning, fit\\-gap analysis, SAP TM system configuration E2E, testing, rollout and post\\-implementation support\n\n\n**Industry Knowledge**\n* Expertise in logistics and supply chain operations across multiple transportation modes (road, rail, ocean, air, intermodal)\n* Knowledge of carrier management practices, freight procurement, contract negotiations, and service level agreements\n* Familiarity with industry best practices, benchmarks, and emerging trends (sustainability, real\\-time visibility, autonomous transportation)\n\n\n**Consulting Competencies**\n* Proven ability to engage with client and support strategic decision\\-making\n* Expertise in requirements gathering through workshops, interviews, and process analysis; translating business needs into technical specifications\n* Change management and organizational adoption strategies, including training program design, communication planning, and stakeholder engagement\n* Project governance frameworks, steering committee management, and escalation resolution\n* Risk management, issue resolution, and proactive communication to ensure on\\-time delivery\n\n\n**To qualify for the role, you must have**\n* Degree in Engineering or MBA in Supply Chain Area.\n* Desired to have SAP certification on SAP TM.\n* Having experience of working in integration area of SAP TM and other areas.\n* Minimum of 5\\-7 years of experience in SAP TM.\n\n\n**What We Look For**\n**What we offer you**\n At EY, we\u2019ll develop you with future\\-focused skills and equip you with world\\-class experiences. We\u2019ll empower you in a flexible environment, and fuel you and your extraordinary talents in a diverse and inclusive culture of globally connected teams.\n   \n\n  \n\n To help create an equitable and inclusive experience during the recruitment process, please inform us as soon as possible about any disability\\-related adjustments or accommodations you may need.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Our Commitment** \n : As a commitment, we persistently endeavour to embody our values, fulfil our purpose, and champion inclusiveness. Our dedication is to cultivate EY into an environment where diverse perspectives are celebrated, creating a supportive atmosphere for individuals to authentically be themselves and contribute their utmost.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Professional Development** \n : From entry\\-level employees to senior leaders, we believe in continuous learning. We offer opportunities to build new skills, take on leadership roles, and connect and grow through mentorship.\n   \n\n  \n\n**People and Culture** \n : In our dynamic workplace, diversity, equity, and inclusiveness are ingrained in our culture. We're united by a commitment to create an environment where every individual's differences are valued, practices are equitable, fostering a sense of belonging. Our shared values include integrity, respect, teaming, inclusiveness, energy, enthusiasm, courage to lead, and building relationships based on doing the right thing.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Benefits** \n : Embark on a transformative career journey with us and indulge in a suite of premium benefits, encompassing exclusive health and wellness packages, enticing rewards, and cutting\\-edge learning opportunities that empower you to continually grow and excel in your professional and personal development.\n   \n\n  \n\n**How to Apply** \n : If you are passionate to join us and are aligned with our commitment to building a better working world, we invite you to apply by completing our user\\-friendly form with personal and professional information and by providing your consent to data privacy.\n   \n\n  \n\n Successful candidates advance to a competency\\-based interview. If mutual interest persists, a job offer awaits.\n   \n\n  \n\n \u201cWe are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to Diversity, Equity \\& Inclusion\u201d.\n   \n\n  \n\n**EY \\| Building a better working world**\n EY is building a better working world by creating new value for clients, people, society and the planet, while building trust in capital markets.\n   \n\n  \n\n Enabl